          <ns0:rules>
            <ns0:rule name="Standard Wargear" id="techmarine-II-std" hidden="false">
              <ns0:description>Power Armour, Bolt Pistol, Power Weapon, Servo-Arm and Frag Grenades.</ns0:description>
            </ns0:rule>
            <ns0:rule name="Legiones Astartes" id="techmarine-II-legiones" hidden="false">
              <ns0:description>Legiones Astartes; also has And They Shall Know No Fear as presented in ProHammer Classic and is not Fearless.</ns0:description>
            </ns0:rule>
            <ns0:rule name="Independent Character" id="techmarine-II-ic" hidden="false">
              <ns0:description>The Legion Techmarine is an Independent Character, subject to Field Team while accompanied by Servo-automata.</ns0:description>
            </ns0:rule>
            <ns0:rule name="Servo-Arm" id="techmarine-II-servoarm" hidden="false">
              <ns0:description>Grants an additional Power Fist-style close-combat attack rolled separately and provides +1 to Battlesmith repair rolls. The normal Battlesmith 5+ therefore succeeds on a 4+ while the Servo-Arm is retained.</ns0:description>
            </ns0:rule>
            <ns0:rule name="Battlesmith" id="techmarine-II-battlesmith" hidden="false">
              <ns0:description>Instead of firing in the Shooting phase, while in base contact with an eligible friendly Vehicle, Cybernetica Cortex model or Iron and Machine model, roll a D6. On a 5+, remove one Engine Damaged, restore one Weapon Destroyed, remove one Immobilised result, or restore one lost Wound to an eligible non-vehicle up to its starting Wounds. One attempt per turn; a model may benefit from only one successful repair per turn. Destroyed models cannot be returned. Daemons may not normally be repaired.</ns0:description>
            </ns0:rule>
            <ns0:rule name="Bolster Defences" id="techmarine-II-bolster" hidden="false">
              <ns0:description>Before either army deploys, nominate one ruin or similar defensive terrain feature wholly or partially within the army's deployment zone. Improve its Cover Save by 1 to a maximum of 3+. A terrain feature may only be Bolstered once.</ns0:description>
            </ns0:rule>
            <ns0:rule name="Field Team" id="techmarine-II-field" hidden="false">
              <ns0:description>If accompanied by one or more Servo-automata, the Techmarine and his Servo-automata form one Field Team. The Techmarine may not voluntarily leave while any Servo-automata remain alive. The whole Field Team may join and leave friendly units as though the Techmarine were an Independent Character. If he is slain, surviving Servo-automata form a unit and become subject to Cybernetica.</ns0:description>
            </ns0:rule>
            <ns0:rule name="Dedicated Transport" id="techmarine-II-transport-rule" hidden="false">
              <ns0:description>If not equipped with a Space Marine Bike, this Techmarine may select a Rhino. If accompanied by Servo-automata, the Rhino is purchased for the entire Field Team.</ns0:description>
            </ns0:rule>
          </ns0:rules>
          <ns0:selectionEntryGroups>
            <ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Wargear" id="techmarine-II-wargear" hidden="false">
              <ns0:entryLinks>
                <ns0:entryLink import="true" name="Auspex" hidden="false" id="techmarine-II-auspex" type="selectionEntry" targetId="gear-auspex">
