Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Hasik Noyan-Khan | 6 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 4 | 10 | 2+/4+
Unit Composition:
LORD OF THE HORDE While Hasik is part of a White Scars unit, that unit has the Stubborn special rule. In addition, the unit may re-roll failed Morale tests. The second result must be accepted. COMMAND RETINUE Hasik may select one Legion Command Squad or Legion Veteran Squad as his retinue. If Hasik is mounted on a Bike or Jetbike, every model in the retinue may purchase a Space Marine Bike for +20 points per model. The selected unit does not occupy a separate Force Organisation slot.
• 1 Hasik Noyan-Khan
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Iron Halo
• Power Weapon
• Bolt pistol
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (White Scars)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• Stubborn
• Lord of the Horde
Allegiance:
• Traitor only
OPTIONS
• Hasik Noyan-Khan may take:
• Krak grenades ................................. +2 points
• Melta bombs .................................. +5 points
• Space Marine Bike ............................ +35 points
• If mounted on a Space Marine Bike, it may be upgraded to a
Jetbike for a further +5 points.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-0-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="2" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Hasik Noyan-Khan may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-1-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-1-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Hasik Noyan-Khan may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Space Marine Bike" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-2-space-marine-bike"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-2-space-marine-bike-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="35" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-2-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Hasik Noyan-Khan may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Jetbike for a further" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-3-jetbike-for-a-further"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-3-jetbike-for-a-further-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-v-8-hasik-noyan-khan-opt-3-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• If mounted on a Space Marine Bike, it may be upgraded to a</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="V — JAGHATAI KHAN, THE WARHAWK" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-v-9-v-jaghatai-khan-the-warhawk"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="490" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-v-9-v-jaghatai-khan-the-warhawk-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-v" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-v-9-v-jaghatai-khan-the-warhawk-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Jaghatai Khan" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-v-9-v-jaghatai-khan-the-warhawk-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-v-9-v-jaghatai-khan-the-warhawk-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the White Scars, the Great Khan, Warhawk of Chogoris
Few among the Primarchs were as difficult to predict or contain as Jaghatai Khan. Raised beneath the open skies of Chogoris, the Great Khan made speed itself a weapon, refusing the ponderous doctrines favoured by many of his brothers in favour of fluid manoeuvre, sudden violence and the freedom to strike wherever the enemy was weakest.
Upon the battlefield Jaghatai was a blur of motion, appearing without warning at the head of his riders before vanishing beyond retaliation. His wars were hunts conducted across continents and worlds, enemy armies slowly encircled and dismembered by forces that seemed never to remain where they were expected. To fight the Khan was not merely to face one of the Emperor's sons, but to attempt to bind the wind itself.
Jaghatai Khan | 8 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 9 | 6 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Jaghatai Khan
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Wildfire Panoply
• White Tiger Dao
• Storm’s Voice
• Cyber-hawk
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (White Scars)
• Master of the Hunt
• Lightning Strike
• Sire of the White Scars
• Ride Beyond the Horizon
WILDFIRE PANOPLY Fashioned to permit its wearer a freedom of movement scarcely conceivable in armour of such strength, the Wildfire Panoply was perfectly suited to the fluid and relentless style of warfare practised by the Great Khan. The Wildfire Panoply counts as Primarch Armour. WHITE TIGER DAO A magnificent curved blade fashioned in the traditions of Chogoris, the White Tiger Dao was wielded by Jaghatai with extraordinary speed and precision. The White Tiger Dao is a Master-crafted Power Weapon. Attacks made with it are resolved at +1 Strength. STORM’S VOICE A finely wrought archaeotech pistol of unknown provenance, Storm’s Voice delivered bursts of destructive energy at close range with devastating effect. Weapon Range S AP Type Storm’s Voice 12" 6 4 Pistol 2, Rending, Concussive, Master-crafted CYBER-HAWK Jaghatai was often accompanied by one of the sophisticated cybernetic hunting birds favoured by the warriors of Chogoris, its augurs identifying prey and transmitting targeting information to nearby warriors. Jaghatai Khan’s Cyber-hawk follows the normal rules for a Cyber-hawk presented in the White Scars Armoury. MASTER OF THE HUNT The Great Khan pursued his enemies with an instinctive understanding of movement and timing, breaking away from battle only to strike again from an unexpected direction. Jaghatai Khan and any Bike or Jetbike unit he has joined gain the Hit &amp; Run special rule. If that unit already possesses Hit &amp; Run, the controlling player may re-roll the dice rolled to determine its Hit &amp; Run movement. The second result must be accepted. LIGHTNING STRIKE The Khan struck with terrifying momentum, committing himself wholly to the instant of attack before passing beyond the reach of retaliation. During an Assault phase in which Jaghatai Khan charged, increase his Strength characteristic by +1 for that Assault phase. SIRE OF THE WHITE SCARS The presence of the Great Khan drove the mounted warriors of the V Legion to feats of speed and horsemanship beyond even their already exceptional abilities. Friendly White Scars Bike and Jetbike units with at least one model within 12" of Jaghatai Khan may re-roll failed Dangerous Terrain tests and failed Hit &amp; Run tests. RIDE BEYOND THE HORIZON Jaghatai understood that no battle line was absolute. When the moment demanded it, the Khan and his riders would disappear from the enemy’s sight entirely, only to return from a direction thought impossible. Once per battle, at the beginning of the White Scars Movement phase, if Jaghatai Khan is mounted on the Sojutsu Pattern Voidbike and has joined a Bike or Jetbike unit, this rule may be used. Remove Jaghatai Khan and the unit he has joined from the battlefield and place them into Ongoing Reserves. They automatically return during the following White Scars turn and must enter play using Outflank. No Reserve roll is required. OPTIONS • Jaghatai Khan may take a Sojutsu Pattern Voidbike ........ +40 points SOJUTSU PATTERN VOIDBIKE The Sojutsu Pattern Voidbike was a machine constructed for the proportions and abilities of a Primarch, allowing the Great Khan to lead even the swiftest formations of the V Legion from the front. If Jaghatai Khan takes a Sojutsu Pattern Voidbike, his Unit Type becomes Jetbike. He follows all normal ProHammer rules for Jetbikes. PRIMARCH RETINUE Jaghatai Khan may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Golden Keshig Squadron A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. If Jaghatai Khan is mounted on the Sojutsu Pattern Voidbike, a Legion Honour Guard Squad selected as his Primarch Retinue may equip every model in the squad with a Jetbike for +35 points per model. Every model in the squad must take this upgrade.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="GREY SLAYER PACK" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="105" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-cat" name="Troops" hidden="false" targetId="cat-troops" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-vi" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Grey Slayer" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Grey Slayer Huscarl" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Grey Slayer | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 8 | 3+
Grey Slayer Huscarl | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Troops
TRUE GRIT A model with True Grit which is equipped with both a Bolter and a Close-combat weapon counts as fighting with two close-combat weapons and therefore receives +1 Attack in close combat. However, that model does not receive the normal +1 Attack for charging. PACK ASSAULT If a Grey Slayer Pack charges an enemy unit which was already engaged with another friendly Space Wolves unit at the beginning of that Assault phase, every Grey Slayer gains +1 Attack during that Assault phase.
Unit Composition:
• 4 Grey Slayers
• 1 Grey Slayer Huscarl
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Grey Slayer Huscarl is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Bolter
• Close-combat weapon
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves)
• True Grit
• Pack Assault
OPTIONS
• The pack may include up to fifteen additional Grey Slayers for +18 points per model.
• Any model may replace its Bolter with:
• Combat Shield ................................. +3 points
• For every five models in the pack, one Grey Slayer may replace his Bolter with:
• Flamer ......................................... +5 points
• Meltagun ...................................... +10 points
• Plasma Gun .................................... +15 points
• For every five models in the pack, one Grey Slayer may replace his Close-combat weapon with:
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• Frost Blade or Frost Axe ..................... +15 points
• Power fist .................................... +15 points
• One model may carry:
• Legion Vexilla ............................... +10 points
• One other model may carry:
• Nuncio Vox ................................... +10 points
• The entire pack may take:
• Frag grenades ............................ +1 point per model
• Krak grenades ........................... +2 points per model
GREY SLAYER HUSCARL
The Grey Slayer Huscarl may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Space Wolves Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
A pack of ten models or fewer may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Combat Shield" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-opt-0-combat-shield"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-opt-0-combat-shield-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="5" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="3" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Any model may replace its Bolter with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Flamer" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-opt-1-flamer"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-opt-1-flamer-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• For every five models in the pack, one Grey Slayer may replace his Bolter with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Meltagun" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-opt-2-meltagun"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-vi-0-grey-slayer-pack-opt-2-meltagun-max" field