</ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-vi-11-vi-leman-russ-the-wolf-king-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Leman Russ" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-11-vi-leman-russ-the-wolf-king-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Freki" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-11-vi-leman-russ-the-wolf-king-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">0</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Geri" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vi-11-vi-leman-russ-the-wolf-king-profile-2"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">0</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-vi-11-vi-leman-russ-the-wolf-king-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the Space Wolves, the Wolf King of Fenris, the Emperor’s Executioner
Leman Russ was the savage king of Fenris and master of the VI Legion, a warrior whose barbarous aspect concealed a keen instinct for war and an unwavering understanding of his purpose. To many he was little more than the Emperor’s attack dog, a role Russ cultivated willingly, for beneath the feasting, boasting and ritual savagery lay one of the Imperium’s most dangerous hunters.
When the Emperor required an enemy brought to heel, Russ and the Rout were unleashed. The Wolf King sought the strongest prey upon the battlefield and pursued it without hesitation, accompanied often by the great Fenrisian wolves Freki and Geri. Against traitors, witches and monsters alike, Russ fought not as a berserker without purpose, but as an executioner who had already judged his prey.
Leman Russ | 8 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 7 | 6 | 10 | 1+
Freki | 5 | 0 | 5 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 5+
Geri | 5 | 0 | 5 | 5 | 2 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 5+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Leman Russ
• Freki
• Geri
Unit Type:
• Leman Russ: Infantry (Character)
• Freki and Geri: Cavalry
Wargear:
Leman Russ:
• Armour Elavagar
• Mjalnar, the Sword of Balenight, the Axe of Helwinter or Krakenmaw
• Scornspitter
• Frag Grenades
Freki and Geri:
• Rending Claws and Fangs
Special Rules:
Leman Russ:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Space Wolves)
• The Emperor’s Executioner
• Preternatural Senses
• The Wolf King
• Bring Me the Traitor
Freki and Geri:
• Fearless
• The Wolves of the Wolf King
Freki:
• Freki the Fierce
Geri:
• Geri the Cunning
RESTRICTIONS
Leman Russ may only be selected for a Loyalist Space Wolves army. He otherwise follows all normal rules and restrictions for Primarchs.
ARMOUR ELAVAGAR Wrought with the runes and protective wards of Fenris, Armour Elavagar protected the Wolf King against threats of both the material world and the powers of the Warp. Armour Elavagar counts as Primarch Armour. Whenever an enemy psychic power directly affects Leman Russ, after the power has been successfully invoked and any normal attempt to Deny the Witch has been resolved, roll a D6. On a roll of 5+, Leman Russ is unaffected by that psychic power. If Russ has joined a unit, the remainder of the unit is affected normally. MJALNAR, THE SWORD OF BALENIGHT Known upon Fenris simply as Mjalnar, the Fang of the Wolf King, the Sword of Balenight was an ancient and sinister weapon whose silver blade darkened with every life it claimed.,Mjalnar is a Master-crafted Power Weapon. Attacks made with it are resolved at +1 Strength and have the Shred special rule. AXE OF HELWINTER A mighty frost axe fashioned using the teeth of one of Fenris’ greatest beasts, Helwinter was capable of splitting armour and war machines beneath the strength of the Wolf King. The Axe of Helwinter is a Power Weapon. Attacks made with it are resolved at +2 Strength and have the Armourbane special rule. KRAKENMAW Wielded by Russ during the earlier years of the Great Crusade, Krakenmaw was a colossal chainsword forged for the strength of a Primarch and fashioned from the monstrous trophies of Fenris. Krakenmaw is a Two-Handed Power Weapon. Attacks made with it are resolved at +2 Strength and have the Shred and Rending special rules. SCORNSPITTER Once a Legion bolter, Scornspitter was rebuilt upon a scale suitable for the Wolf King and transformed into a brutally effective sidearm. Weapon Range S AP Type Scornspitter 12" 4 3 Assault 3, Rending RENDING CLAWS AND FANGS Freki and Geri are monstrous examples of the great wolves of Fenris, capable of tearing through armour and flesh with equal savagery. Rending Claws and Fangs count as a single Close Combat Weapon with the Rending special rule. THE EMPEROR’S EXECUTIONER Russ was not merely a warrior, but a weapon wielded against those the Emperor deemed beyond redemption. Once the Wolf King had marked his prey, escape was seldom possible. Before deployment, nominate one enemy Primarch, Independent Character or Monstrous Creature as Russ’ Prey. Leman Russ may re-roll To Hit and To Wound rolls of 1 when making attacks against his Prey. PRETERNATURAL SENSES The instincts of the Wolf King bordered upon the supernatural. Ambush, darkness and concealment offered little protection against a hunter raised among the death-world predators of Fenris. Leman Russ has the Night Vision special rule. In addition, enemy units deploying using Infiltrate may never be deployed within 18" of Leman Russ or a unit he has joined, regardless of line of sight. THE WOLF KING To fight beneath the gaze of Russ was to stand beside the lord of Fenris himself, and few warriors of the Rout would allow themselves to falter before their gene-sire. Friendly Space Wolves units with at least one model within 12" of Leman Russ may re-roll failed Break Tests. In addition, they may re-roll failed Leadership Tests made when using the Counter-Attack special rule. The second result must be accepted. BRING ME THE TRAITOR Once Russ had scented his quarry, little could restrain him from closing upon it. If Russ’ nominated Prey is within 12" of him at the beginning of the Space Wolves Movement phase, Leman Russ may immediately move D6" towards that model before making his normal move. This is a bonus move and does not prevent Russ from moving, shooting or charging normally later in the turn. Russ must end this bonus move closer to his Prey than he began it. THE WOLVES OF THE WOLF KING Freki and Geri were no ordinary beasts, but the legendary wolf-brothers of Leman Russ and constant companions of the King of Fenris. Freki and Geri begin the battle as part of Leman Russ’ unit and may never voluntarily leave him. They do not prevent Leman Russ from using his Independent Character rules or joining another friendly unit. Whenever Russ joins or leaves a unit, Freki and Geri accompany him. If Russ selects a Primarch Retinue, Freki and Geri are also part of that unit. For Transport Capacity, Freki and Geri each count as two models. FREKI THE FIERCE Of the two great wolves, Freki was the more openly savage, hurling himself upon the foe with terrifying violence. During an Assault phase in which Freki charged, he gains +1 Attack in addition to the normal bonus for charging. GERI THE CUNNING Where Freki overwhelmed his prey through fury, Geri was a patient and calculating hunter, instinctively seeking the weaknesses of the greatest quarry. During each Assault phase, when Geri directs his attacks against an enemy Independent Character or Monstrous Creature, he may re-roll one failed To Hit roll OR one failed To Wound roll. The second result must be accepted. PRIMARCH RETINUE Leman Russ may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. Freki and Geri accompany Leman Russ regardless of which Primarch Retinue is selected.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="TEMPLAR BRETHREN SQUAD" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vii-0-templar-brethren-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="135" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-vii-0-templar-brethren-squad-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-vii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Templar Brethren" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vii-0-templar-brethren-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+/6+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Templar Champion" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-vii-0-templar-brethren-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+/6+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-vii-0-templar-brethren-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Templar Brethren | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 9 | 3+/6+
Templar Champion | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+/6+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
RIGHTEOUS ZEAL Whenever the squad would normally take a Morale test for suffering 25% or more casualties from enemy shooting, it may instead move D6" directly towards the nearest visible enemy unit. This movement may not bring any model within 1" of an enemy model and does not count as charging or Falling Back. If no enemy unit is visible, take the Morale test normally.
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 4 Templar Brethren
• 1 Templar Champion
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Templar Champion is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Combat Shield
• Bolt pistol
• Rending Weapon
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Imperial Fists)
• Stubborn
• Righteous Zeal
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Templar Brethren for +27 points per model.
• Up to five models may replace their Rending Weapon with:
