• Master of Defence
• This Ground Shall Not Fall
AURIC ARMOUR Fashioned in gold and bearing the heraldry of the VII Legion, Dorn’s armour was a masterwork of protection befitting the Praetorian of Terra. Auric Armour counts as Primarch Armour. STORM’S TEETH A colossal chainsword constructed for the strength of a Primarch, Storm’s Teeth tore through armour, flesh and fortification with the same relentless brutality its master brought to war. Storm’s Teeth is a Two-Handed Power Weapon. Attacks made with it are resolved at +2 Strength and have the Shred and Rampage special rules. VOICE OF TERRA Presented to Dorn in recognition of his station as Praetorian, the Voice of Terra was a magnificent bolter of Custodes manufacture, built to a scale and quality worthy of a Primarch. Weapon Range S AP Type Voice of Terra 24" 5 4 Salvo 3/5, Rending THE UNYIELDING Rogal Dorn possessed an endurance and implacability legendary even amongst the Primarchs. Blows that might have felled another warrior were met with little more than grim determination. Rogal Dorn may re-roll Armour Saves of 1. The second result must be accepted. LORD CASTELLAN Under Dorn’s command, defensive positions became bastions and retreat was contemplated only when no other course remained. Friendly Imperial Fists units with at least one model within 12" of Rogal Dorn gain the Stubborn special rule. A unit which already has Stubborn may instead re-roll failed Pinning tests while within 12" of Dorn. MASTER OF DEFENCE Few warriors understood the defence of a position as completely as Rogal Dorn, and those who attempted to overwhelm a line commanded by the Praetorian often found themselves advancing directly into carefully prepared fields of fire. Rogal Dorn and any unit he has joined count as being equipped with Frag Grenades when assaulted through Difficult Terrain. In addition, Dorn and any unit he has joined may make an Overwatch attack when charged even if another rule or circumstance would normally prevent that unit from doing so. THIS GROUND SHALL NOT FALL Where Dorn chose to make his stand, earthworks were strengthened, firing lanes calculated and every available defence transformed into part of a greater fortress. After terrain has been placed but before either army deploys, nominate up to two Fortifications, ruins or other suitable defensive terrain features wholly or partially within the Imperial Fists deployment zone. The Cover Save provided by each nominated terrain feature is improved by 1, to a maximum of 3+. Friendly Imperial Fists units occupying either nominated terrain feature may not be Pinned. These benefits last for the duration of the battle. PRIMARCH RETINUE Rogal Dorn may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Huscarl Terminator Retinue • Templar Brethren Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. A Huscarl Terminator Retinue selected for Rogal Dorn ignores any normal requirement for the accompanying Character to wear Terminator Armour.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="TERROR SQUAD" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="150" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-viii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Terror Marine" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Headsman" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Terror Marine | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Headsman | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 9 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Terror Marines
• 1 Headsman
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Headsman is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Bolter
• Bolt pistol
• Chainsword
• Frag grenades
• Trophies of Judgement
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Night Lords)
• Infiltrate
• Preferred Enemy (Infantry)
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Terror Marines
for +25 points per model.
• Any model may replace his Chainsword with:
• Rending Weapon ................................ +5 points
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• Any model may replace his Bolter with:
• Volkite Charger .............................. +10 points
• For every five models in the squad, one Terror Marine may
replace his Bolter with:
• Flamer ......................................... +5 points
• Rotor Cannon ................................. +10 points
• Heavy Flamer ................................. +10 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ............................ +2 points per model
• Melta bombs .............................. +5 points per model
• Stealth Adept ............................ +1 point per model
HEADSMAN
The Headsman may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Night Lords
Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Additional model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-additional"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-additional-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="5" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Additional model" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-additional-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>May include up to 5 additional models at +25 points each, as stated in the source entry.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="for" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-opt-0-for"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-opt-0-for-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The squad may include up to five additional Terror Marines</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Rending Weapon" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-opt-1-rending-weapon"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-viii-0-terror-squad-opt