"true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Konrad Curze" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-viii-9-viii-konrad-curze-the-night-haunter-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-viii-9-viii-konrad-curze-the-night-haunter-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the Night Lords, the Night Haunter, the King of Terrors
Konrad Curze was terror given flesh. Raised alone in the lightless cities of Nostramo, he learned from childhood that fear could accomplish what armies often could not, and carried that lesson into command of the VIII Legion. Worlds which might have resisted conventional conquest were broken by exemplary atrocity, their populations forced into obedience by the certainty that the Night Lords would make resistance unbearable.
Yet behind the calculated horror lay a mind tormented by visions of futures yet to come. Curze fought with an almost supernatural awareness of danger, moving through battle with the terrible certainty of one who had already witnessed the blows meant to kill him. When the Night Haunter descended upon weakened prey, few escaped his blades or the terror that followed in his wake.
Konrad Curze | 8 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 8 | 6 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Konrad Curze
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Nightmare Mantle
• Mercy &amp; Forgiveness
• Widowmakers
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Night Lords)
• Psyker (Mastery Level 1\)
• King of Terrors
• Bloody Murder
• Night Haunter
• Dark Precognition
NIGHTMARE MANTLE A macabre suit of artificer-wrought plate adorned with trophies and the imagery of death, the Nightmare Mantle transformed the already monstrous figure of Curze into the embodiment of the terror he sought to inspire. The Nightmare Mantle counts as Primarch Armour. MERCY &amp; FORGIVENESS Mercy and Forgiveness were the paired blades of the Night Haunter, weapons wielded with horrifying speed and precision to tear apart those Curze had marked for death. Mercy and Forgiveness are a matched pair of Master-crafted Power Weapons. Attacks made with them are resolved at Curze’s normal Strength and have the Shred and Rending special rules. They count as two close combat weapons. WIDOWMAKERS The Widowmakers were a collection of exquisitely balanced throwing blades which Curze could cast with such accuracy that even heavily protected victims might be slain before realising they had been targeted. Weapon Range S AP Type Widowmakers 12" 4 5 Assault 3, Lethal Precision LETHAL PRECISION On an unmodified To Wound roll of 6, a Wound inflicted by the Widowmakers allows neither Armour nor Invulnerable Saves. Cover Saves may be taken normally. KING OF TERRORS Few beings in the Imperium inspired terror as instinctively as the Night Haunter. Even hardened warriors could find their courage failing when confronted by the certainty of his approach. Enemy units with at least one model within 12" of Konrad Curze suffer -2 Leadership. Models and units with the Fearless special rule are unaffected by this penalty. NIGHT HAUNTER Curze struck from darkness and confusion, disappearing from the enemy's grasp almost as quickly as he descended upon them. Konrad Curze has the Stealth and Hit &amp; Run special rules. In the Movement Phase, Curze moves as though he were Jump Infantry, despite not being equipped with a Jump Pack. This does not change his Unit Type or grant him Deep Strike, Bulky, Swift, or any other special rules normally associated with Jump Infantry. DARK PRECOGNITION Curze was plagued throughout his life by visions of events yet to come. Though these revelations were fragmented and beyond his conscious control, in battle they could grant the Night Haunter an uncanny awareness of threats before they occurred. The first successful To Hit roll made against Konrad Curze during each player turn must be re-rolled. The second result must be accepted. In addition, Konrad Curze is a Psyker (Mastery Level 1\) and knows only the Precognition psychic power from the Divination discipline. Whenever Curze attempts to invoke Precognition, he takes the Psychic Test using Leadership 8 instead of his normal Leadership characteristic. All other rules for invoking Precognition, including Perils of the Warp and Disturbance in the Warp, apply normally. PRIMARCH RETINUE Konrad Curze may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Atramentar Flay-Clade • Night Raptor Squad • Terror Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. NIGHT RAPTOR RETINUE: If Konrad Curze selects a Night Raptor Squad as his Primarch Retinue, the unit may use his Hit &amp; Run special rule while he remains part of the unit.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="DAWNBREAKER COHORT" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-ix-0-dawnbreaker-cohort"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="210" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-ix-0-dawnbreaker-cohort-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-ix" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Dawnbreaker" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-ix-0-dawnbreaker-cohort-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Dawnbreaker Champion" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-ix-0-dawnbreaker-cohort-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-ix-0-dawnbreaker-cohort-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Dawnbreaker | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+
Dawnbreaker Champion | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 10 | 2+
