• Melta bombs ...................................... +5 points</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xii-11-delvarus-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xii-11-delvarus-opt-0-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xii-11-delvarus-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="2" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xii-11-delvarus-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Kargos may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xii-11-delvarus-opt-1-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xii-11-delvarus-opt-1-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xii-11-delvarus-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Kargos may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XII — ANGRON, THE RED ANGEL" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xii-12-xii-angron-the-red-angel"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="515" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xii-12-xii-angron-the-red-angel-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xii-12-xii-angron-the-red-angel-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Angron" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xii-12-xii-angron-the-red-angel-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xii-12-xii-angron-the-red-angel-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the World Eaters, Lord of the Red Sands, the Red Angel
Angron was violence incarnate, a Primarch broken upon the killing fields of Nuceria long before the Emperor found him. The cybernetic Butcher’s Nails driven into his brain transformed anger into agony and battle into the only fleeting relief from an existence of constant pain. When command of the XII Legion was given to him, the warriors who would become the World Eaters were reshaped in their father’s image.
In battle Angron cared little for manoeuvre, subtlety or the preservation of his own warriors. He sought the enemy with single-minded fury, crashing into their lines with Gorefather and Gorechild roaring in his hands. With every death the Nails drove him deeper into frenzy, until friend and foe alike risked falling beneath the Red Angel’s blades.
Angron | 9 | 6 | 7 | 6 | 6 | 7 | 6 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Angron
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Armour of Mars
• Gorefather &amp; Gorechild
• Spite Furnace
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (World Eaters)
• The Red Angel
• Butcher’s Nails
• Sire of the World Eaters
• The Nails Demand Blood
ARMOUR OF MARS Forged for the Primarch of the XII Legion, the Armour of Mars was a brutal and functional panoply, scarred by countless battles and designed to endure the punishment Angron willingly sought. The Armour of Mars counts as Primarch Armour. GOREFATHER &amp; GORECHILD Taken from the gladiatorial traditions of Nuceria and reforged for the strength of a Primarch, Gorefather and Gorechild were monstrous chainaxes whose roaring teeth could tear through flesh, armour and war machines alike. Gorefather and Gorechild are a matched pair of Power Weapons. Attacks made with them are resolved at +1 Strength and have the Shred and Armourbane special rules. Gorefather and Gorechild count as two close combat weapons. SPITE FURNACE A brutal plasma weapon carried by Angron into the thickest fighting, Spite Furnace was little more than another means by which the Red Angel could kill before closing with his prey. Weapon Range S AP Type Spite Furnace 12" 7 2 Pistol, Gets Hot, Master-crafted THE RED ANGEL Once battle was joined, little could divert Angron from the nearest source of bloodshed. Strategy gave way to the demands of the Nails and the overwhelming need to close with the foe. If Angron is able to declare a charge during the Assault phase, he must do so. Angron and any unit he has joined may declare charges against enemy units up to 8" away instead of the normal 6". They must charge the closest eligible enemy unit to Angron. If two or more eligible units are equally close, the World Eaters player may choose between them. Difficult Terrain does not reduce this charge distance, although Dangerous Terrain is resolved normally. BUTCHER’S NAILS The archeotech implants driven into Angron’s brain transformed pain, rage and violence into an inseparable whole. In battle they drove the Primarch beyond exhaustion and reason, but his fury did not always distinguish friend from foe. Angron has the Furious Charge special rule. Angron may never voluntarily Withdraw from close combat. Whenever Angron rolls an unmodified 1 To Hit in close combat, that attack instead strikes another friendly model in Angron’s unit. The roll of 1 may not be re-rolled. Resolve the hit using Angron’s current Strength and all rules of the close combat weapon he is using. If more than one eligible friendly model is present, the opposing player chooses which model is struck. The friendly model may take any saves normally permitted. Wounds inflicted in this manner do not count towards the close combat result. If Angron is not accompanied by another friendly model, the roll of 1 is simply a miss. SIRE OF THE WORLD EATERS The warriors of the XII Legion saw in Angron the ultimate expression of the violence they had been taught to embrace. His presence drove them onward, demanding that victory in close combat be followed only by further slaughter. Friendly World Eaters units with at least one model within 12" of Angron add +1 to all Pursuit rolls. In addition, such units may re-roll failed Break Tests caused by losing a close combat. The second result must be accepted. THE NAILS DEMAND BLOOD The more Angron killed, the deeper the Nails drove him into frenzy. Each slaughter merely fed the need for another, until the Red Angel became an unstoppable engine of destruction. Each time an enemy unit is completely destroyed during an Assault phase in a close combat involving Angron, increase Angron’s Attacks characteristic by +1 for the remainder of the battle. This bonus is cumulative, to a maximum of +3 Attacks. Thus Angron’s Attacks characteristic may increase from 6 to a maximum of 9. These additional Attacks remain for the rest of the battle. OPTIONS • Angron may exchange Gorefather &amp; Gorechild for Widowmaker ........ Free WIDOWMAKER An immense weapon dating from the earlier campaigns of the Great Crusade, Widowmaker traded the murderous speed of Angron’s paired axes for sheer crushing power. Widowmaker is a Two-Handed Power Weapon. Attacks made with Widowmaker are resolved at Strength 10 and have the Armourbane special rule. All attacks made with Widowmaker are resolved at -2 Initiative. PRIMARCH RETINUE Angron may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Devourer Terminator Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="ANGRON, THE RED ANGEL" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xii-13-angron-the-red-angel"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="650" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xii-13-angron-the-red-angel-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xii-13-angron-the-red-angel-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Angron, the Red Angel" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xii-13-angron-the-red-angel-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4++</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xii-13-angron-the-red-angel-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Daemon Primarch of Khorne
Angron’s ascension did not free him from rage; it made rage the entirety of his existence. Where once stood a broken Primarch now rampages the Red Angel, a towering incarnation of slaughter whose coming must be purchased in blood. As the World Eaters butcher their foes in close combat, Angron is drawn ever nearer to the material realm. When at last he descends, the madness of the Nails spreads across the battlefield until restraint, discipline and reason are drowned beneath an all-consuming desire to kill.
Angron, the Red Angel | 9 | 5 | 8 | 7 | 8 | 7 | 8 | 10 | 2+/4++
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Angron, the Red Angel
Unit Type:
• Monstrous Creature (Character)
Wargear:
• Blades of the Red Angel
• Daemonic Armour
Special Rules:
• Daemon
• Fear
• Fearless
• Fleet
• Furious Charge
• Eternal Warrior
• Adamantium Will
• Master of the Legion
• Daemonic Flight
• Blood Calls to Blood
• The Red Angel Descends
• The Nails Sing
RESTRICTIONS
Angron, the Red Angel may only be selected for a World Eaters army. An army may not include both Angron, the Red Angel and Angron in his mortal form.
DAEMONIC FLIGHT Angron may move up to 12" during the Movement phase and may move over intervening models and terrain while doing so. Angron may never join another unit and no model may join him. BLADES OF THE RED ANGEL The Blades of the Red Angel count as a pair of Master-crafted Power Weapons. Angron receives the normal +1 Attack for fighting with two close-combat weapons. Against Vehicles, attacks made with the Blades of the Red Angel have Armourbane. Against Monstrous Creatures and models with Toughness 6 or greater, Angron may re-roll failed To Wound rolls. BLOOD CALLS TO BLOOD Angron may never begin the battle on the battlefield and does not make normal Reserve rolls. Instead, keep a cumulative total of all unsaved Wounds inflicted upon enemy models by friendly World Eaters models in close combat. Only Wounds actually suffered count. Excess Wounds beyond those a model had remaining do not count. Wounds caused by shooting or psychic shooting attacks never contribute. At the end of each World Eaters Assault phase, consult the following table: Wounds Inflicted Summoning Roll 0–9 Cannot be summoned 10–19 6+ 20–29 5+ 30–39 4+ 40–49 3+ 50+ 2+ If successful, Angron arrives at the beginning of the controlling player’s next turn. If Angron has not previously been summoned, he automatically arrives at the beginning of Turn 5. THE RED ANGEL DESCENDS When Angron arrives, deploy him using the Deep Strike rules. Angron does not scatter. Angron may declare a charge during the same turn in which he arrives. Unlike a normal model charging after Deep Strike, Angron retains all bonus Attacks and other benefits normally gained for charging. THE NAILS SING While Angron is on the battlefield, all units gain +1 Attack during the first round of a close combat in which they charged. In addition, any unit composed entirely of models wearing Power Armour or Artificer Armour may declare charges against enemies up to 8" away instead of 6". These benefits affect friend and foe alike. World Eaters suffer the following additional effects: Compulsory Charge: If an eligible enemy unit is within charge distance, a World Eaters unit must charge the nearest eligible enemy unit. No Restraint: A World Eaters unit which wins a close combat must Pursue an enemy which Falls Back. This overrides rules which would normally prevent that unit from Pursuing unless a Pursuit is physically or mission-wise impossible. Bloodward Consolidation: If the opposing unit is destroyed and no Pursuit is possible, the World Eaters unit must Consolidate as directly as possible towards the nearest enemy unit. The Attack granted by The Nails Sing is cumulative with the normal charge bonus and the World Eaters’ Blood Frenzy.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="INVICTARUS SUZERAIN SQUAD" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="225" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xiii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Invictarus Suzerain" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Suzerain Legate" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Invictarus Suzerain | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+/5+
Suzerain Legate | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 2+/5+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
SUZERAIN LEGATE The Suzerain Legate is a Character and may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury. LEGATINE AXE A Legatine Axe is a Power Weapon which grants +1 Strength. A model attacking with a Legatine Axe does not receive the bonus Attack for fighting with two close-combat weapons. HONOUR GUARD One Invictarus Suzerain Squad may be selected as the retinue of an Ultramarines Praetor or named Ultramarines Independent Character who is permitted to select a Command Squad. The Suzerains do not occupy a separate Force Organisation slot. The character and Suzerains count as a single HQ selection.
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 5 Invictarus Suzerains
Unit Type:
• Infantry
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Boarding Shield
• Bolt pistol
• Legatine Axe
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
• Stubborn
• Honour Guard
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Invictarus Suzerains for +45 points per model.
• The entire squad may take:
• Frag grenades ............................ +1 point per model
• Krak grenades ........................... +2 points per model
• Melta bombs ............................. +5 points per model
• One Invictarus Suzerain may be upgraded to:
• Suzerain Legate ................................. +20 points</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Additional model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-additional"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-additional-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="5" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="45" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Additional model" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-additional-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>May include up to 5 additional models at +45 points each, as stated in the source entry.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Frag grenades (base unit; +1 pts/model)" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-0-frag-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-0-frag-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The entire squad may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule name="Squad-wide cost note" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-0-squadwide" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The source prices this option at +1 points per model. The displayed selection charges the parsed base unit only; apply the same per-model surcharge for any additional models selected.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades (base unit; +2 pts/model)" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-1-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-1-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="10" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The entire squad may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule name="Squad-wide cost note" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-1-squadwide" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The source prices this option at +2 points per model. The displayed selection charges the parsed base unit only; apply the same per-model surcharge for any additional models selected.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs (base unit; +5 pts/model)" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-2-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-2-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-2-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The entire squad may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule name="Squad-wide cost note" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-2-squadwide" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The source prices this option at +5 points per model. The displayed selection charges the parsed base unit only; apply the same per-model surcharge for any additional models selected.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Suzerain Legate" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-3-suzerain-legate"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-3-suzerain-legate-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="20" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xiii-0-invictarus-suzerain-squad-opt-3-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• One Invictarus Suzerain may be upgraded to:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="FULMENTARUS TERMINATOR SQUAD" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="325" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xiii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Fulmentarus Terminator" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Fulmentarus Decurion" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Fulmentarus Terminator | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+/4+
Fulmentarus Decurion | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 5 | 3 | 9 | 2+/4+
Force Organisation:
GUIDED WARHEADS When firing Frag missiles from their Cyclone Missile Launchers, Fulmentarus Terminators may fire at an enemy unit they cannot see if that unit is visible to a friendly model equipped with a Nuncio Vox. The Nuncio Vox bearer may not be embarked in a Vehicle, Falling Back, Pinned or engaged in close combat. Cyclone Missile Launchers firing in this manner: • Must use Frag missiles. • Count as Barrage weapons. • Follow the normal ProHammer rules for Barrage fire. Krak missiles may not use Guided Warheads.
• Elites
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 5 Fulmentarus Terminators
Unit Type:
• Infantry
Wargear:
• Cataphractii Terminator Armour
• Storm bolter
• Power fist
• Cyclone Missile Launcher
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
• Guided Warheads
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Fulmentarus Terminators for +65 points per model.
• Any model may replace his Power fist with:
• Chainfist ........................................ +5 points
• One Fulmentarus Terminator may be upgraded to:
• Fulmentarus Decurion ........................... +20 points
• The Fulmentarus Decurion may take:
• Grenade Harness ................................ +10 points
The Fulmentarus Decurion may select up to 50 points of permitted Terminator weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
A squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Additional model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-additional"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-additional-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="5" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="65" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Additional model" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-additional-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>May include up to 5 additional models at +65 points each, as stated in the source entry.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Chainfist" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-opt-0-chainfist"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-opt-0-chainfist-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="10" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xiii-1-fulmentarus-terminator-squad-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Any model may replace his Power fist with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Fulmentarus Decurion" hidden="false" i