• Independent Character
• Psyker (Mastery Level 2\)
• Legion Support Officer
• Psychic Savant
OPTIONS
• Titus Prayto may take:
• Krak grenades ................................... +2 points</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-8-titus-prayto-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-8-titus-prayto-opt-0-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-8-titus-prayto-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="2" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xiii-8-titus-prayto-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Titus Prayto may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XIII — ROBOUTE GUILLIMAN, THE AVENGING SON" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="500" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xiii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="allegiance-loyalist" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Roboute Guilliman" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiii-9-xiii-roboute-guilliman-the-avenging-son-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the Ultramarines, Lord of Ultramar, the Avenging Son
Roboute Guilliman was among the greatest commanders and statesmen of the Great Crusade, a Primarch whose genius lay not merely in winning battles, but in understanding the greater structure of war itself. Under his rule the worlds of Ultramar became a realm of extraordinary order and prosperity, while the XIII Legion grew into one of the largest and most disciplined forces of the Legiones Astartes.
Upon the battlefield Guilliman sought neither reckless glory nor rigid adherence to a single doctrine. Every engagement was studied, every success and failure considered, and theory was continually tested against the practical realities of war. His warriors were expected to adapt as swiftly as their Primarch, changing formation and method as circumstances demanded until the enemy was confronted with precisely the form of warfare it was least prepared to resist.
Roboute Guilliman | 7 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 5 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Roboute Guilliman
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Armour of Reason
• Gladius Incandor
• Hand of Dominion
• Arbitrator
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Ultramarines)
• Master Strategist
• Preternatural Strategy
• Sire of Ultramar
• Theoretical / Practical
RESTRICTIONS
Roboute Guilliman may only be selected for a Loyalist Ultramarines army. He otherwise follows all normal rules and restrictions for Primarchs.
ARMOUR OF REASON A magnificent suit of war-plate fashioned according to the exacting requirements of the Primarch of the XIII Legion, the Armour of Reason combined formidable protection with the sophisticated command systems required to direct vast armies across the battlefield. The Armour of Reason counts as Primarch Armour. GLADIUS INCANDOR A superbly balanced blade wielded with the calculated precision that characterised Guilliman’s approach to war, Gladius Incandor was equally suited to the destruction of armoured warriors and monstrous foes. Gladius Incandor is a Master-crafted Power Weapon. Attacks made with it are resolved at +1 Strength and have the Shred special rule. HAND OF DOMINION A colossal powered gauntlet constructed for the strength of a Primarch, the Hand of Dominion could crush armour and tear apart even the heaviest engines of war. The Hand of Dominion is a Master-crafted Power Fist with the Armourbane special rule. ARBITRATOR Arbitrator was a master-crafted bolter fashioned to the proportions of the Primarch of the XIII Legion, capable of delivering exceptionally powerful and accurate fire. Weapon Range S AP Type Arbitrator 18" 6 3 Assault 2, Rending, Master-crafted MASTER STRATEGIST Few commanders possessed Guilliman’s ability to comprehend the flow of an entire battlefield and translate that understanding into precise orders. Unless a rule specifically states otherwise, the range of Roboute Guilliman’s special rules which affect friendly Ultramarines units is 18". PRETERNATURAL STRATEGY Guilliman’s ability to reassess a battle plan in moments allowed the XIII Legion to alter its dispositions even as the enemy committed itself to battle. After both armies have deployed but before the first turn begins, nominate one friendly Ultramarines unit. That unit may be redeployed anywhere it could legally have been deployed at the beginning of the battle. It must obey all normal deployment restrictions and may not be placed into Reserve unless it was already eligible to begin the battle in Reserve. SIRE OF ULTRAMAR The warriors of the XIII Legion fought beneath the gaze of a Primarch who demanded discipline in victory and adversity alike. Friendly Ultramarines units with at least one model within 12" of Roboute Guilliman may re-roll failed Morale tests. The second result must be accepted. THEORETICAL / PRACTICAL To Guilliman, no doctrine was valuable merely because it had succeeded before. Theory existed to be tested in battle, and practical experience existed to refine theory. At the beginning of each Ultramarines turn, choose one of the following doctrines. The chosen doctrine affects friendly Ultramarines units with at least one model within 18" of Roboute Guilliman until the beginning of the next Ultramarines turn. ADVANCE Affected units may move up to 1" further than normal during their Movement phase. FIRE Affected units may re-roll shooting To Hit rolls of 1. ASSAULT Affected units may re-roll close combat To Hit rolls of 1. PRIMARCH RETINUE Roboute Guilliman may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Invictarus Suzerain Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="DEATHSHROUD TERMINATORS" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="110" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xiv" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Deathshroud" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Deathshroud | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+/5+
SILENT RETINUE A Death Guard character who would normally be permitted to select a Legion Terminator Command Squad may instead select one Deathshroud Terminator Squad as his retinue. The Deathshroud do not occupy a separate Force Organisation slot. The character and Deathshroud count as a single HQ selection.
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 2 Deathshroud Terminators
Unit Type:
• Infantry
Wargear:
• Terminator Armour
• Manreaper
• Alchem Flamer
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Death Guard)
• Fearless
• Silent Retinue
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Deathshroud Terminators for +55 points per model.
• The entire squad may exchange its Terminator Armour for Cataphractii Terminator Armour at no additional cost.
If this option is selected, the squad instead has a 2+/4+ Save and follows all normal rules and restrictions for Cataphractii Terminator Armour.
• The entire squad may take:
• Melta bombs .............................. +5 points per model
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Additional model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-additional"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-additional-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="5" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="55" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Additional model" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-additional-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>May include up to 5 additional models at +55 points each, as stated in the source entry.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs (base unit; +5 pts/model)" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-opt-0-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-opt-0-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="10" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The entire squad may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule name="Squad-wide cost note" id="r41-unit-xiv-0-deathshroud-terminators-opt-0-squadwide" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The source prices this option at +5 points per model. The displayed selection charges the parsed base unit only; apply the same per-model surcharge for any additional models selected.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="GRAVE WARDEN TERMINATOR SQUAD" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-1-grave-warden-terminator-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="250" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xiv-1-grave-warden-terminator-squad-cat" name="Heavy Support" hidden="false" targetId="cat-heavy" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xiv" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Grave Warden" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-1-grave-warden-terminator-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Chem-master" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xiv-1-grave-warden-terminator-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xiv-1-grave-warden-terminator-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Grave Warden | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+/4+
Chem-master | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 9 | 2+/4+
Force Organisation:
• Heavy Support
Unit Composition:
SHROUDED IN DEATH A Grave Warden Terminator Squad counts as being equipped with Defensive Grenades. All normal ProHammer rules for Defensive Grenades apply. Grave Warden Weapons Weapon Range S AP Type Assault Grenade Launcher — Krak 18" 6 4 Assault 2 Assault Grenade Launcher — Toxin 18" 1 5 Assault 4, Poisoned (3+), Ignores Cover Death Cloud Projector Template 1 4 Assault 1, Poisoned (3+), Ignores Cover
• 4 Grave Wardens
• 1 Chem-master
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Chem-master is a Character
Wargear:
