Allegiance:
• Traitor only
OPTIONS
• Ashurhaddon may take:
• Krak grenades ................................... +2 points
• Melta bombs .................................... +5 points</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-9-vheren-ashurhaddon-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-9-vheren-ashurhaddon-opt-0-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvi-9-vheren-ashurhaddon-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="2" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xvi-9-vheren-ashurhaddon-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Ashurhaddon may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-9-vheren-ashurhaddon-opt-1-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvi-9-vheren-ashurhaddon-opt-1-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xvi-9-vheren-ashurhaddon-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Ashurhaddon may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="FALKUS KIBRE" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-10-falkus-kibre"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="28" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xvi-10-falkus-kibre-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xvi" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvi-10-falkus-kibre-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Falkus Kibre" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-10-falkus-kibre-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvi-10-falkus-kibre-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Falkus Kibre | 5 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 3 | 9 | 2+/4+
One Justaerin Terminator may be upgraded to Falkus Kibre for +28 points. Falkus therefore has a total cost of 85 points. Falkus: • remains part of the Justaerin Terminator Squad; • is a Character; • is not an Independent Character; • occupies no separate Force Organisation selection. Wargear: • Cataphractii Terminator Armour • The normal weapons carried by the Justaerin he replaces OPTIONS Falkus may select any normal Justaerin weapon replacement, paying the listed cost. He may not select a Heavy weapon. Special Rules: • Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus) • Justaerin Primus JUSTAERIN PRIMUS While Falkus Kibre remains alive, his Justaerin Terminator Squad has the Fearless special rule. In addition, the squad may purchase the Furious Charge Veteran Skill for +4 points per model.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="TARIK TORGADDON" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="105" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon-cat" name="HQ" hidden="false" targetId="cat-hq" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xvi" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Tarik Torgaddon" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Tarik Torgaddon | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 5 | 3 | 9 | 2+/5+
One of the following units may replace its Sergeant with Tarik Torgaddon:
• Legion Veteran Squad
• Legion Tactical Squad containing 20 models
Torgaddon has a total cost of 105 points. Do not also pay the normal cost of the Sergeant he replaces.
Torgaddon:
• remains part of the squad for the entire battle;
• is a Character;
• is not an Independent Character;
• occupies no separate Force Organisation selection.
No Independent Character may join Torgaddon's squad.
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Refractor Field
• Bolter
• Power weapon
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)
• Stubborn
OPTIONS
• Torgaddon may take:
• Krak grenades ................................... +2 points</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon-opt-0-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="2" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xvi-11-tarik-torgaddon-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Torgaddon may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XVI — HORUS LUPERCAL, THE WARMASTER" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-12-xvi-horus-lupercal-the-warmaster"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="525" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xvi-12-xvi-horus-lupercal-the-warmaster-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xvi" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvi-12-xvi-horus-lupercal-the-warmaster-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Horus Lupercal" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-12-xvi-horus-lupercal-the-warmaster-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvi-12-xvi-horus-lupercal-the-warmaster-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the Sons of Horus, the Warmaster, First Among Equals
Horus Lupercal was the favoured son of the Emperor and the greatest commander of the Great Crusade. Raised to the rank of Warmaster above all his brother Primarchs, Horus possessed not only formidable personal prowess but a genius for command, diplomacy and the decisive application of overwhelming force. Under his leadership the XVI Legion became the spearpoint of the Imperium’s greatest conquests, its warriors striking directly at the heart of an enemy before resistance could properly form.
When Horus took to the field, he did so at the centre of a war machine without equal. The black-armoured Justaerin formed his inner circle, elite formations descended in sudden decapitation strikes, and high above the battlefield waited the guns of the Vengeful Spirit. Whether as the glorious Warmaster of the Great Crusade or the architect of the rebellion that would tear the Imperium apart, Horus was a commander around whom entire wars revolved.
Horus Lupercal | 8 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Horus Lupercal
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Serpent’s Scales
• Worldbreaker
• The Talon of Horus
• Frag Grenades
• Krak Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)
• Will of the Warmaster
• Master of the Speartip
• The First Company
• The Vengeful Spirit
SERPENT’S SCALES The Serpent’s Scales were a magnificent suit of artificer-wrought Terminator plate constructed for the Warmaster, incorporating defensive systems and technologies available to few warriors of the Imperium. The Serpent’s Scales count as Primarch Armour. WORLDBREAKER A colossal mace gifted to Horus by Ferrus Manus, Worldbreaker was fashioned to match the Warmaster’s immense strength and could crush warriors and engines of war beneath its blows. Worldbreaker is a Master-crafted Thunder Hammer. When Horus attacks with Worldbreaker, he resolves his attacks at Initiative 3 instead of Initiative 1. All other Thunder Hammer rules apply normally. THE TALON OF HORUS Perhaps the most infamous weapon borne by the Warmaster, the Talon of Horus combined a massive powered claw with an incorporated Storm Bolter supplied with specialised ammunition from the arsenals of the XVI Legion. In close combat, the Talon of Horus follows all the normal rules for a Master-crafted Lightning Claw. The Talon also incorporates a Twin-linked Storm Bolter. Each time Horus fires the Storm Bolter, choose one of the ammunition profiles below. Weapon Range S AP Type Banestrike 18" 4 4 Assault 2, Twin-linked, Banestrike Dragonfire 24" 4 5 Assault 2, Twin-linked, Ignores Cover Hellfire 24" X 5 Assault 2, Twin-linked, Poisoned (2+) Kraken 30" 4 4 Assault 2, Twin-linked Vengeance 18" 4 3 Assault 2, Twin-linked, Gets Hot BANESTRIKE A natural To Wound roll of 6 made with Banestrike Ammunition is resolved at AP3. Only one ammunition type may be used each time the Talon is fired. The effects of different ammunition types may never be combined. Firing the incorporated Storm Bolter does not prevent Horus from using either the Talon of Horus or Worldbreaker during the following Assault phase. WILL OF THE WARMASTER Horus was not merely the commander of the XVI Legion, but Warmaster of the Emperor’s armies. His presence could steady an entire battle line and drive his sons onwards through fire that would break lesser warriors. Any friendly unit with the Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus) special rule which can draw line of sight to Horus may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests. Friendly units with the Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus) special rule with at least one model within 12" of Horus instead have the Fearless special rule. Will of the Warmaster is Horus’ unique Warlord ability. He does not select a normal Warlord Trait. MASTER OF THE SPEARTIP None understood the decapitation strike better than Horus. Under his command the spearhead of the XVI Legion struck with even greater weight, committing several elite formations at the decisive point before the enemy could react. When using the Sons of Horus Tip of the Spear special rule, up to two Sons of Horus Infantry units selected from Elites may deploy using Deep Strike instead of the normal one. The Independent Character allowance granted by Tip of the Spear is unchanged. All units deployed in this manner must obey the normal requirements of Tip of the Spear and begin the battle in Reserve. THE FIRST COMPANY The black-armoured warriors of the First Company formed the deadliest core of the Warmaster’s assaults, and when Horus took to the field they were often committed in overwhelming numbers. Up to two Legion Terminator Squads in an army containing Horus may be selected as Troops choices instead of Elites choices. One of these two selections may instead be a Justaerin Terminator Squad. A Justaerin Terminator Squad selected as Troops in this manner does not count against the normal 0–1 limitation on Justaerin Terminator Squads. Legion Terminator Squads and Justaerin Terminator Squads selected as Troops through this rule may fulfil compulsory Troops selections. THE VENGEFUL SPIRIT The Warmaster did not descend upon a battlefield unsupported. High above him hung the Vengeful Spirit, flagship of the XVI Legion and the centre of one of the greatest expeditionary hosts ever assembled. An army containing Horus receives the following benefits: SPEARHEAD ASSAULT Reduce the points cost of every Legion Drop Pod and Anvillus Pattern Dreadclaw Drop Pod purchased by the army by 10 points. This reduction does not alter any other restrictions, Transport Capacity or special rules of those vehicles. ORBITAL BOMBARDMENT Once per battle, from the second turn onwards, Horus may call down a Lance Strike from the Vengeful Spirit during his Shooting phase. Horus must be on the battlefield and may not be engaged in close combat or a Primarch Duel. Calling down the bombardment is made instead of Horus making a normal shooting attack during that Shooting phase. Weapon Range S AP Type Vengeful Spirit Lance Strike Unlimited 10 1 Ordnance 1, Blast Place the Blast marker anywhere on the battlefield. No line of sight is required. Roll the Scatter die. If a Hit is rolled, the marker remains in place. If an arrow is rolled, the marker scatters D6" in the direction shown. PRIMARCH RETINUE Horus Lupercal may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Justaerin Terminator Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. A Justaerin Terminator Squad selected as Horus’ Primarch Retinue: • does not count against the normal 0–1 limitation on Justaerin Terminator Squads; • gains Furious Charge at no additional points cost; • may purchase any upgrades normally available to a Justaerin Terminator Squad, including Falkus Kibre where otherwise permitted. GREAT CRUSADE PANOPLY — OPTIONAL To represent Horus during the earlier Great Crusade, before he came to bear the infamous weapons most closely associated with the Heresy, Horus may exchange Worldbreaker and the Talon of Horus for: • Master-crafted Power Sword • Master-crafted Seeker Bolter with Special Issue Ammunition This option reduces Horus’ points cost by 25 points. MASTER-CRAFTED SEEKER BOLTER Each time Horus fires the Master-crafted Seeker Bolter, select one of the following profiles: Weapon Range S AP Type Dragonfire Bolts 24" 4 5 Rapid Fire, Ignores Cover, Master-crafted Hellfire Bolts 24" X 5 Rapid Fire, Poisoned (2+), Master-crafted Kraken Bolts 30" 4 4 Rapid Fire, Master-crafted Vengeance Rounds 18" 4 3 Rapid Fire, Gets Hot, Master-crafted Only one ammunition type may be used each time the weapon is fired.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XVI — HORUS ASCENDED, THE WARMASTER" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-13-xvi-horus-ascended-the-warmaster"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="725" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xvi-13-xvi-horus-ascended-the-warmaster-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xvi" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvi-13-xvi-horus-ascended-the-warmaster-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Horus Ascended" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvi-13-xvi-horus-ascended-the-warmaster-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvi-13-xvi-horus-ascended-the-warmaster-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the Sons of Horus, Warmaster, Vessel of the Four
At the height of the Siege of Terra, Horus Lupercal had become something greater and more terrible than even a Primarch. Empowered by all four Gods of Chaos, the Warmaster stood as the supreme champion of the Traitor host, possessed of unnatural strength, resilience and speed while the powers of the Warp themselves bent to his will.
Horus Ascended | 9 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Horus Ascended
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Serpent's Scales
• Worldbreaker
• The Talon of Horus
• Frag Grenades
• Krak Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)
• Will of the Warmaster
• Master of the Speartip
• The First Company
• The Vengeful Spirit
• Vessel of the Four
• Favoured of the Dark Gods
• Blessings of the Four
• The Warmaster Must Lead
SERPENT'S SCALES The Serpent's Scales confer Horus a 1+ Armour Save and 3+ Invulnerable Save. WORLDBREAKER Worldbreaker is a Master-crafted Thunder Hammer. Horus strikes with Worldbreaker at Initiative 4 rather than Initiative 1. All other Thunder Hammer rules apply normally. THE TALON OF HORUS The Talon counts as a Master-crafted Lightning Claw and grants +1 Strength. It incorporates a Twin-linked Storm Bolter which may use any ammunition from his previous Entry Horus may divide his Attacks between Worldbreaker and the Talon of Horus in any combination. WILL OF THE WARMASTER Friendly Sons of Horus units with line of sight to Horus may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests. Friendly Sons of Horus units with at least one model within 12" of Horus are Fearless. MASTER OF THE SPEARTIP When Horus commands the army, one additional eligible Sons of Horus Elite unit may use the Legion's Tip of the Spear deployment rule. THE FIRST COMPANY Horus may take a Justaerin Terminator Squad as his retinue instead of a normal Command Squad or Terminator Command Squad. Legion Terminators and Justaerin also receive any additional availability granted by the Sons of Horus army list while Horus is present. THE VENGEFUL SPIRIT Drop Pods and Dreadclaws in Horus' army use the reduced costs specified by the Sons of Horus army list. Once per battle, Horus may call down a Lance Strike in his Shooting phase: Weapon Range Str AP Type Lance Strike Unlimited 10 1 Ordnance 1, Blast Resolve this using the normal rules for an Orbital Strike. VESSEL OF THE FOUR Horus counts as a Daemon for all rules, weapons and abilities which specifically affect Daemons. Horus is considered to bear the favour of all four Chaos Gods, but receives no additional characteristic bonuses from Blessings of the Four; these bonuses are already incorporated into his profile. FAVOURED OF THE DARK GODS Whenever an enemy psychic power directly targets or affects Horus, roll a D6 after the Psychic Test is passed. On a 3+, the power is nullified and has no effect upon him. A power which instead directly targets or affects a friendly unit within 6" of Horus is nullified on a 4+. BLESSINGS OF THE FOUR If Horus Ascended is included in the army, Traitor Legiones Astartes Infantry units and Independent Characters may purchase one Blessing of Chaos. A unit may possess only one Blessing, and every model in the unit must purchase the same Blessing. Primarchs may not purchase Blessings. Blessing Unit Cost Independent Character Effect Khorne +5 pts/model +20 pts +1 Attack Slaanesh +4 pts/model +15 pts +1 Initiative Nurgle +7 pts/model +25 pts +1 Toughness and Slow and Purposeful Tzeentch +8 pts/model +25 pts Gain a 5++ save, or improve an existing Invulnerable Save by 1, to a maximum of 4++ The Blessing of Nurgle may not be purchased by Bikes, Jetbikes or Jump Infantry. THE WARMASTER MUST LEAD Horus Ascended may never voluntarily begin the battle in Reserve and must be deployed at the start of the battle whenever the mission permits. If a mission requires Horus to begin in Reserve, he automatically arrives on the first turn.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="COVENANT ZEALOT MOB" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-0-covenant-zealot-mob"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="80" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xvii-0-covenant-zealot-mob-cat" name="Troops" hidden="false" targetId="cat-troops" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xvii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Covenant Zealot" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-0-covenant-zealot-mob-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">6+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Legion Overseer" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-0-covenant-zealot-mob-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+/5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvii-0-covenant-zealot-mob-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Covenant Zealot | 3 | 3 | 3 | 3 | 1 | 3 | 1 | 7 | 6+
Legion Overseer | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+/5+
SPECIAL RULES DRIVEN TO SLAUGHTER While the Legion Overseer is alive, the Covenant Zealot Mob is Fearless and ignores all Leadership penalties. If the unit is able to declare a charge against an enemy unit during the Assault Phase, it must declare a charge. If more than one enemy unit may be charged, the controlling player may choose which enemy unit is charged. During an Assault Phase in which the unit charges, all Covenant Zealots gain +1 Attack and +1 Initiative for that Assault Phase. The Legion Overseer does not receive these bonuses. If the Legion Overseer is slain, the unit immediately loses Fearless and Driven to Slaughter for the remainder of the battle. If the unit is not locked in close combat when the Overseer is slain, it immediately becomes Pinned. If the unit is locked in close combat, it becomes Pinned as soon as that combat ends, provided it is still on the battlefield. Once the unit recovers from being Pinned, it functions normally and uses its own Leadership for all subsequent tests. EXPANDABILE Casualties suffered by a Covenant Zealot Mob, or the destruction of the unit, never cause friendly units to take Morale, Leadership or Pinning tests.
Force Organisation:
• Troops
• Word Bearers only
Unit Composition:
• 10 Covenant Zealots
• 1 Legion Overseer
Unit Type:
