acteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvii-11-hol-beloth-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Hol Beloth | 6 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 4 | 10 | 2+/4+
TAINTED WEAPON Hol Beloth's Tainted Weapon follows the normal rules presented in the Word Bearers Armoury. HEXAGLYPHIC WARD The first unsaved Wound suffered by Hol Beloth during the battle is ignored. If that attack would inflict a Massive Wound, the Ward is used before rolling the D3 Wounds. After preventing one Wound, the Ward has no further effect. EXHORTATION OF BATTLE Once per battle, at the beginning of a Word Bearers Assault phase, Hol Beloth may declare an Exhortation of Battle. Until the end of that Assault phase, Word Bearers models with a Weapon Skill lower than 5 count as having Weapon Skill 5. Models which already have Weapon Skill 5 or higher are unaffected. COMMAND RETINUE Hol Beloth may select one Legion Command Squad as his retinue. The selected squad does not occupy a separate Force Organisation slot.
Force Organisation:
• HQ
Allegiance:
• Traitor only
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Iron Halo
• Master-crafted Power Fist
• Tainted Weapon
• Plasma pistol
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• Hexaglyphic Ward
• Exhortation of Battle
OPTIONS
• Hol Beloth may take:
• Krak grenades ................................ +2 points
• Melta bombs ................................. +5 points</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-11-hol-beloth-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-11-hol-beloth-opt-0-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvii-11-hol-beloth-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="2" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xvii-11-hol-beloth-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Hol Beloth may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-11-hol-beloth-opt-1-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvii-11-hol-beloth-opt-1-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xvii-11-hol-beloth-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Hol Beloth may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XVII — LORGAR AURELIAN, THE URIZEN" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-12-xvii-lorgar-aurelian-the-urizen"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="460" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xvii-12-xvii-lorgar-aurelian-the-urizen-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xvii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="allegiance-traitor" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xvii-12-xvii-lorgar-aurelian-the-urizen-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Lorgar Aurelian" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xvii-12-xvii-lorgar-aurelian-the-urizen-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvii-12-xvii-lorgar-aurelian-the-urizen-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the Word Bearers, the Urizen, Bearer of the Word
Lorgar Aurelian was a warrior, prophet and conqueror whose greatest weapon was never the strength of his arm, but the power of belief. Raised amidst the temples and holy wars of Colchis, Lorgar sought meaning and divinity in a universe the Emperor had commanded mankind to view through reason alone. Under his rule the XVII Legion became not merely soldiers of conquest, but missionaries of an ever-changing faith.
Upon the battlefield the Urizen fought surrounded by warriors whose devotion bordered upon fanaticism. His words could turn hesitation into certainty and sacrifice into sacred duty, while the great crozius Illuminarum served as both weapon and symbol of his authority. After embracing the Primordial Truth, however, the powers long dormant within Lorgar awakened, transforming the once-reluctant warrior into a formidable sorcerer in his
Lorgar Aurelian | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | 5 | 6 | 5 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Lorgar Aurelian
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Armour of the Word
• Illuminarum
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Word Bearers)
• Voice of the Urizen
• Fanatical Devotion
• Dark Oratory
ARMOUR OF THE WORD Covered in Colchisian scripture, protective wards and passages of Lorgar’s own writings, the Armour of the Word was both a magnificent suit of war-plate and a physical manifestation of the Primarch’s faith. The Armour of the Word counts as Primarch Armour. Enemy Psykers suffer -1 Leadership when taking a Psychic Test to invoke a psychic power which directly targets Lorgar or a unit he has joined. ILLUMINARUM Forged by Ferrus Manus and gifted to Lorgar, Illuminarum was an immense crozius whose design would later echo through the weapons carried by the Chaplains of the Legiones Astartes. Illuminarum is a Master-crafted Power Weapon. Attacks made with Illuminarum are resolved at +2 Strength and have the Concussive special rule. Lorgar may also use Illuminarum to make a Smash attack using the normal ProHammer rules. VOICE OF THE URIZEN Lorgar possessed an extraordinary gift for oratory, capable of inspiring absolute devotion in those who heard him speak. Friendly Word Bearers units with at least one model within 12" of Lorgar may re-roll failed Morale and Pinning tests. The second result must be accepted. FANATICAL DEVOTION Those who fought beside Lorgar did so in the presence of their gene-sire, prophet and spiritual master. To retreat from his side was unthinkable. A friendly Word Bearers unit joined by Lorgar has the Fearless special rule while he remains part of that unit. DARK ORATORY With scripture, invocation and carefully chosen words, Lorgar could transform the fury of his sons into something approaching religious ecstasy. At the beginning of each Word Bearers turn, nominate one friendly Word Bearers unit with at least one model within 12" of Lorgar. Until the beginning of the next Word Bearers turn, that unit may re-roll close combat To Hit rolls of 1. Only one unit may benefit from Dark Oratory at a time. OPTIONS • Lorgar may be upgraded to Lorgar Transfigured ........ +75 points LORGAR TRANSFIGURED After embracing the Primordial Truth and surrendering himself fully to the powers he had once only dimly perceived, Lorgar unlocked the psychic potential that had long remained dormant within him. This upgrade may only be selected in a Traitor Word Bearers army. Lorgar Transfigured gains the following rules: • Psyker (Mastery Level 3\) • Psychic Ascendancy • Illuminarum becomes a Force Weapon PSYKER — MASTERY LEVEL 3 Lorgar Transfigured selects three psychic powers before the battle. Each power may be selected from either of the following ProHammer psychic disciplines: • Divination • Telekinesis Any combination of the two disciplines may be used. Lorgar otherwise follows all normal ProHammer rules for a Mastery Level 3 Psyker. PSYCHIC ASCENDANCY The Warp no longer answered Lorgar reluctantly. What had once been uncertain intuition became conscious sorcery wielded with terrifying conviction. Lorgar Transfigured may ignore the first -1 Leadership penalty he would suffer from Disturbance in the Warp during each player turn. Further Disturbance in the Warp penalties apply normally. ILLUMINARUM — TRANSFIGURED When wielded by Lorgar Transfigured, Illuminarum additionally counts as a Force Weapon. It retains its Master-crafted, +2 Strength, Concussive and Smash rules. After Lorgar inflicts one or more unsaved Wounds with Illuminarum, he may attempt to activate it using the normal ProHammer rules for Force Weapons. PRIMARCH RETINUE Lorgar Aurelian may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Gal Vorbak Dark Brethren A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. Gal Vorbak Dark Brethren may only be selected as Lorgar’s Primarch Retinue in a Traitor army.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="FIREDRAKE TERMINATOR SQUAD" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="285" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xviii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Firedrake" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Firedrake Master" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Firedrake | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 2+/5+
Firedrake Master | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 10 | 2+/5+
Force Organisation:
DRAGONSCALE STORM SHIELD A model equipped with a Dragonscale Storm Shield has a 4+ Invulnerable Save in close combat and against shooting attacks made with Flame or Melta weapons. Against all other shooting attacks, the shield provides a 5+ Invulnerable Save. FIREDRAKE RETINUE A Firedrake Terminator Squad may be selected as the retinue of a Salamanders Praetor wearing Terminator Armour, Artellus Numeon or another Character whose rules specifically permit it. The squad does not occupy a separate Elites selection.
• Elites
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 4 Firedrakes
• 1 Firedrake Master
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Firedrake Master is a Character
Wargear:
• Terminator Armour
• Thunder hammer
• Dragonscale Storm Shield
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Salamanders)
• Stubborn
• Implacable Advance
• Firedrake Retinue
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Firedrakes for +45 points per model.
• Any model may upgrade his Thunder hammer to a Master-crafted Thunder hammer for +10 points.
• For every five models in the squad, up to two Firedrakes may replace their Dragonscale Storm Shield with:
• Heavy Flamer ................................. +10 points
• Multi-Melta .................................. +20 points
The Firedrake Master may select up to 50 points of permitted Terminator weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Salamanders Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Additional model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-additional"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-additional-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="5" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="45" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Additional model" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-additional-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>May include up to 5 additional models at +45 points each, as stated in the source entry.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Heavy Flamer" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-opt-0-heavy-flamer"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-opt-0-heavy-flamer-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="2" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="10" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• For every five models in the squad, up to two Firedrakes may replace their Dragonscale Storm Shield with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Multi-Melta" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-opt-1-multi-melta"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-opt-1-multi-melta-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="2" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="20" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xviii-0-firedrake-terminator-squad-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• For every five models in the squad, up to two Firedrakes may replace their Dragonscale Storm Shield with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="PYROCLAST SQUAD" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="190" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xviii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Pyroclast" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Pyroclast Warden" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Pyroclast | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 9 | 2+
Pyroclast Warden | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 10 | 2+
Force Organisation:
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Pyroclasts
• 1 Pyroclast Warden
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Pyroclast Warden is a Character
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Pyroclast Flame Projector
• Bolt pistol
• Close-combat weapon
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Salamanders)
• Stubborn
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Pyroclasts for +30 points per model.
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ............................ +2 points per model
• Melta bombs .............................. +5 points per model
PYROCLAST WARDEN
The Pyroclast Warden may replace his Close-combat weapon with:
• Rending Weapon ................................ +5 points
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• Power fist .................................... +15 points
• Thunder hammer ............................... +20 points
The Pyroclast Warden may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Salamanders Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.
PYROCLAST FLAME PROJECTOR Each time a Pyroclast Flame Projector is fired, choose one of the following: • It may fire as a Salamanders Heavy Flamer. • It may fire as a Meltagun. The selected weapon uses all of its normal rules. For the purposes of Promethean Cult and Fire-based Warfare, the weapon counts as the weapon whose profile it is using.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Additional model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-additional"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-additional-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="5" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="30" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Additional model" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-additional-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>May include up to 5 additional models at +30 points each, as stated in the source entry.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades (base unit; +2 pts/model)" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-0-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="10" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The entire squad may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule name="Squad-wide cost note" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-0-squadwide" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The source prices this option at +2 points per model. The displayed selection charges the parsed base unit only; apply the same per-model surcharge for any additional models selected.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs (base unit; +5 pts/model)" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-1-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-1-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The entire squad may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule name="Squad-wide cost note" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-1-squadwide" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The source prices this option at +5 points per model. The displayed selection charges the parsed base unit only; apply the same per-model surcharge for any additional models selected.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Rending Weapon" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-2-rending-weapon"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-1-pyroclast-squad-opt-2-rending-weapon-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id