• Keeper of the Forge
OPTIONS
• T'Kell may take:
• Krak grenades ................................ +2 points
• Melta bombs ................................. +5 points
MASTER ARTIFICER After both armies have been selected but before deployment, choose one friendly Salamanders Character. One weapon carried by that Character becomes Master-crafted for the duration of the battle. Alternatively, one friendly Salamanders Vehicle or Dreadnought may receive Extra Armour at no additional points cost. KEEPER OF THE FORGE One Salamanders Vehicle or Dreadnought eligible to purchase Reinforced Ceramite may receive that upgrade at no points cost. This may not be applied to a Land Raider or Spartan. FORGEFATHER T'Kell receives +2 rather than +1 to Battlesmith attempts for his Servo-Arm. A Battlesmith attempt may still never be improved beyond 3+.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-9-forgefather-t-kell-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-9-forgefather-t-kell-opt-0-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-9-forgefather-t-kell-opt-0-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="2" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xviii-9-forgefather-t-kell-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• T'Kell may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-9-forgefather-t-kell-opt-1-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-9-forgefather-t-kell-opt-1-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xviii-9-forgefather-t-kell-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• T'Kell may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XVIII — VULKAN, THE FORGEFATHER" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-10-xviii-vulkan-the-forgefather"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="520" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xviii-10-xviii-vulkan-the-forgefather-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xviii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="allegiance-loyalist" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xviii-10-xviii-vulkan-the-forgefather-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Vulkan" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xviii-10-xviii-vulkan-the-forgefather-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xviii-10-xviii-vulkan-the-forgefather-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the Salamanders, the Forgefather, Lord of Drakes
Vulkan was among the mightiest and most enduring of the Emperor’s sons, a giant even by the standards of the Primarchs and a craftsman without equal among the Legiones Astartes. Raised upon the volcanic world of Nocturne, he learned that strength existed not for its own sake, but for the protection of those unable to defend themselves. This creed would shape both Vulkan and the XVIII Legion throughout the Great Crusade.
Upon the battlefield the Forgefather advanced with the inevitability of a living fortress, clad in armour of his own making and bearing weapons wrought by his hand. Fire and melta washed harmlessly across drake-scale and ceramite, while Dawnbringer shattered armoured warriors and engines of war beneath its blows. Even death itself seemed unable to claim Vulkan permanently, for the Primarch possessed a regenerative vitality whose limits neither his brothers nor the enemies of mankind fully understood.
Vulkan | 7 | 6 | 7 | 7 | 7 | 5 | 5 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Vulkan
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Draken Scale
• Kesare’s Mantle
• Dawnbringer
• Furnace’s Heart
• Gauntlet of the Forge
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Salamanders)
• The Forgefather
• Lord of Drakes
• Sire of the Salamanders
• Perpetual
RESTRICTIONS
Vulkan may only be selected for a Loyalist Salamanders army. He otherwise follows all normal rules and restrictions for Primarchs.
DRAKEN SCALE A peerless suit of artificer-wrought armour created by Vulkan’s own hand, the Draken Scale combined the finest technologies of the Imperium with the craft traditions of Nocturne. The Draken Scale counts as Primarch Armour. KESARE’S MANTLE Fashioned from the hide of one of Nocturne’s mightiest drakes, Kesare’s Mantle possessed an extraordinary resistance to heat and flame. When resolving an attack made with a Flame weapon against Vulkan, reduce the Strength of that attack by 1, to a minimum of Strength 1. DAWNBRINGER One of the greatest weapons ever forged by Vulkan, Dawnbringer was an immense warhammer whose blows could shatter fortifications, armoured vehicles and even the mightiest living foes. Dawnbringer is a Master-crafted, Two-Handed Power Weapon. Attacks made with Dawnbringer are resolved at Strength 10 and have the Armourbane and Concussive special rules. Any unsaved Wound inflicted by Dawnbringer against a model without the Primarch special rule becomes a Massive Wound and inflicts D3 Wounds instead of one Wound. FURNACE’S HEART A unique energy weapon fashioned by Vulkan, Furnace’s Heart projected a concentrated blast capable of burning through even the finest armour. Weapon Range S AP Type Furnace’s Heart 18" 6 2 Assault 1, Rending, Master-crafted GAUNTLET OF THE FORGE Built directly into Vulkan’s armour, the Gauntlet of the Forge projected torrents of superheated flame capable of reducing infantry to ash. Weapon Range S AP Type Gauntlet of the Forge Template 6 4 Assault 1, Flame THE FORGEFATHER Vulkan was perhaps the greatest smith among the Primarchs, and every weapon he carried had been fashioned or perfected according to his own exacting standards. All ranged and close-combat weapons carried by Vulkan count as Master-crafted. This benefit is already included in the profiles of weapons where relevant. LORD OF DRAKES Born beneath the burning skies of Nocturne, Vulkan could endure heat and fire which would destroy even another transhuman warrior. Vulkan may re-roll failed Armour and Invulnerable Saves made against attacks from Flame or Melta weapons. The second result must be accepted. SIRE OF THE SALAMANDERS The warriors of the XVIII Legion drew strength from the example of their Primarch, enduring the enemy’s fury with the same stubborn determination taught upon Nocturne. Friendly Salamanders units with at least one model within 12" of Vulkan may re-roll failed Morale tests. In addition, such units may re-roll Armour Save rolls of 1 made against attacks from Flame weapons. The second result must be accepted. PERPETUAL The true nature of Vulkan’s extraordinary regenerative ability was unknown even to many of his brother Primarchs. Wounds which should have brought final death could instead prove only a temporary defeat. The first time Vulkan is reduced to 0 Wounds, roll a D6 before removing him as a casualty. On a roll of 4+, Vulkan is not removed. Instead, immediately roll a D3 and restore Vulkan to that many Wounds. Vulkan remains exactly where he was and, if he was engaged in close combat, remains engaged. On a roll of 1–3, Vulkan is removed as a casualty normally. Perpetual may only be used once per battle. If Vulkan successfully uses Perpetual, he is not considered to have been slain for the purposes of Victory Points, Warlord objectives or Price of Failure. Price of Failure and any other rewards for slaying Vulkan are only awarded if Vulkan is ultimately removed as a casualty. PRIMARCH RETINUE Vulkan may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Firedrake Terminator Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="MOR DEYTHAN SQUAD" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="120" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-cat" name="Elites" hidden="false" targetId="cat-elites" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xix" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Mor Deythan" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">8</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Mor Deythan Sergeant" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Mor Deythan | 4 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 8 | 3+
Mor Deythan Sergeant | 4 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Force Organisation:
FATAL STRIKE Once per battle, at the beginning of the Raven Guard Shooting phase, nominate one enemy unit within 18" and line of sight of the Mor Deythan Squad. Until the end of that Shooting phase, models in the squad may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 and To Wound rolls of 1 against the nominated enemy unit. Against Vehicles, re-roll Armour Penetration rolls of 1 instead of To Wound rolls.
• Elites
Unit Composition:
• 4 Mor Deythan
• 1 Mor Deythan Sergeant
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• Mor Deythan Sergeant is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Sniper Rifle
• Bolt pistol
• Close-combat weapon
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Raven Guard)
• Infiltrate
• Move Through Cover
• Fatal Strike
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Mor Deythan for +24 points per model.
• Any model may replace its Sniper Rifle with:
• Combi-flamer ................................ +10 points
• Combi-meltagun .............................. +15 points
• Combi-plasma gun ............................ +15 points
• Combi-volkite charger ....................... +10 points
• For every five models in the squad, one Mor Deythan may replace his Sniper Rifle with:
• Heavy bolter ................................ +15 points
• Missile launcher ............................ +20 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ........................... +2 points per model
• Shroud Bombs ................................. +20 points
• The Mor Deythan Sergeant may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Additional model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-additional"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-additional-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="5" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="24" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Additional model" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-additional-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>May include up to 5 additional models at +24 points each, as stated in the source entry.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Combi-flamer" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-opt-0-combi-flamer"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-opt-0-combi-flamer-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="10" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="10" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• Any model may replace its Sniper Rifle with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Combi-meltagun" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xix-0-mor-deythan-squad-opt-1-combi-meltagun"><ns0:constrai