may replace his Bolter with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Plasma Gun" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-4-plasma-gun"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-4-plasma-gun-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="2" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="15" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-4-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• For every five models, one Effrit may replace his Bolter with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Artificer Armour" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-5-artificer-armour"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-5-artificer-armour-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="10" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-5-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The Effrit Principal may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Venom Spheres" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-6-venom-spheres"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-6-venom-spheres-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xx-3-effrit-disruption-cadre-opt-6-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The Effrit Principal may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="ARMILLUS DYNAT" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-4-armillus-dynat"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="185" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xx-4-armillus-dynat-cat" name="HQ" hidden="false" targetId="cat-hq" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xx" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-4-armillus-dynat-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Armillus Dynat" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-4-armillus-dynat-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xx-4-armillus-dynat-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Armillus Dynat | 6 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 2+/4+
COMMAND SQUAD Dynat may be accompanied by a Legion Command Squad, Legion Terminator Command Squad or Lernaean Terminator Squad. Dynat and the selected squad count as a single HQ selection. THE HARROWING Dynat and any unit he has joined gain Counter-Attack. In addition, models in that unit add +1 to Armour Penetration rolls made against Vehicles in close combat. WEAPON MASTERY Dynat may divide his close-combat attacks between his Power weapon and Thunder hammer in any combination he chooses. Any bonus Attacks received for charging or fighting with two close-combat weapons may also be divided between the two weapons.
Armillus Dynat may be selected as an HQ choice in an Alpha
Legion Detachment.
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Iron Halo
• Power weapon
• Thunder hammer
• Bolt pistol
• Nuncio Vox
• Frag grenades
• Krak grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• The Harrowing
• Weapon Mastery</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="EXODUS" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="110" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-cat" name="HQ" hidden="false" targetId="cat-hq" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xx" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Exodus" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Exodus | 5 | 6 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Exodus may be selected as an HQ choice in an Alpha LegionDetachment.
LONE KILLER Exodus may never join another unit and no Independent Character may join him. He may not fulfil a compulsory HQ selection and may never be the army's Warlord. DEADSHOT Before the battle begins, nominate one enemy Independent Character or unit-upgrade Character. When Exodus fires at a unit containing that model, successful Wounds caused by Exodus may be allocated to the nominated model before other casualties, provided it is within range and line of sight. All Attacks are made at Ap 2. EXECUTE THE MANDATE If the enemy Warlord is slain by an attack made by Exodus, the Alpha Legion player receives an additional 50 Victory Points.
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• M.40 Targeter and Stalker Bolter
• Bolt pistol
• Combat Blade
• Cameleoline
• Frag grenades
• Krak grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)
• Infiltrate
• Move Through Cover
• Scout
• Lone Killer
• Deadshot
• Execute the Mandate
OPTIONS
Exodus may take:
• Melta bombs ...................................... +5 points
• Power Dagger ..................................... +5 points
• Venom Spheres .................................... +5 points</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-0-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-0-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Exodus may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Power Dagger" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-1-power-dagger"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-1-power-dagger-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Exodus may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Venom Spheres" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-2-venom-spheres"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-2-venom-spheres-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r41-unit-xx-5-exodus-opt-2-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Exodus may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="AUTILON SKORR" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-6-autilon-skorr"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="135" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xx-6-autilon-skorr-cat" name="HQ" hidden="false" targetId="cat-hq" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xx" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-6-autilon-skorr-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Autilon Skorr" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-6-autilon-skorr-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/5+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xx-6-autilon-skorr-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Autilon Skorr | 5 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 2+/5+
Autilon Skorr may be selected as an HQ choice in a Traitor Alpha Legion Detachment.
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Refractor Field
• Bolt pistol
• Rime-shard
• Frag grenades
• Krak grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• Delegatus
• Desperate for Glory
DELEGATUS Autilon Skorr counts as a Legion Delegatus Consul for all rules and restrictions. DESPERATE FOR GLORY Once per battle, at the beginning of any Alpha Legion turn, Skorr may invoke Desperate for Glory. Until the beginning of the next Alpha Legion turn, Skorr and any unit he has joined gain Fearless and Feel No Pain (5+). RIME-SHARD Rime-shard counts as a Master-crafted Power Weapon. Attacks made with Rime-shard are resolved at +2 Strength. Rime-shard is Two-handed and therefore does not grant the bonus Attack for fighting with two close-combat weapons.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="INGO PECH" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-7-ingo-pech"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="175" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xx-7-ingo-pech-cat" name="HQ" hidden="false" targetId="cat-hq" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xx" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-7-ingo-pech-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Ingo Pech" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-7-ingo-pech-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xx-7-ingo-pech-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Ingo Pech | 6 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 2+/4+
Ingo Pech may be selected as an HQ choice in an Alpha Legion Detachment.
COMMAND SQUAD Pech may be accompanied by a Legion Command Squad, Legion Terminator Command Squad, Lernaean Terminator Squad or Legion Seeker Squad. Pech and the selected squad count as a single HQ selection. MASTER OF DECEIT An army containing Ingo Pech may use The Rewards of Treachery rule presented in The Coils of the Hydra Rite of War even if the army is not using that Rite. If the army is already using The Coils of the Hydra, Ingo Pech does not permit a second Rewards of Treachery unit.
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Iron Halo
• Power weapon
• Bolter
• Nuncio Vox
• Frag grenades
• Krak grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• Master of Deceit</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="MATHIAS HERZOG" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-8-mathias-herzog"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="170" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xx-8-mathias-herzog-cat" name="HQ" hidden="false" targetId="cat-hq" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xx" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-8-mathias-herzog-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Mathias Herzog" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-8-mathias-herzog-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xx-8-mathias-herzog-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Mathias Herzog | 6 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 3 | 10 | 2+/4+
Mathias Herzog may be selected as an HQ choice in an Alpha Legion Detachment.
FALSE DISPOSITION After both armies have deployed but before determining which player takes the first turn, nominate Herzog and one other friendly non-Vehicle Alpha Legion unit. Both units may immediately be redeployed anywhere wholly within the Alpha Legion deployment zone. Units placed in Reserve or using Infiltrate are not eligible. HEADHUNTER COMMANDER One Headhunter Kill Team may be selected without occupying an Elites choice in an army containing Mathias Herzog. That unit remains an Elites unit for all other purposes.
Wargear:
• Artificer Armour
• Iron Halo
• Bolter with Banestrike Ammunition
• Bolt pistol
• Power weapon
• Frag grenades
• Krak grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)
• Independent Character
• Master of the Legion
• False Disposition
• Headhunter Commander</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="SHEED RANKO" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-9-sheed-ranko"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="110" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xx-9-sheed-ranko-cat" name="HQ" hidden="false" targetId="cat-hq" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xx" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-9-sheed-ranko-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Sheed Ranko" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-9-sheed-ranko-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">3</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">9</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">2+/4+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xx-9-sheed-ranko-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Sheed Ranko | 5 | 5 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 4 | 3 | 9 | 2+/4+
Sheed Ranko may replace one model in a Lernaean Terminator Squad. His total cost is 110 points, meaning the upgrade costs +62 points in addition to the replaced Lernaean Terminator. Ranko remains part of the squad, is not an Independent Character and does not occupy a separate Force Organisation choice.
HYDRA'S RESILIENCE While Sheed Ranko remains alive, his Lernaean Terminator Squad has the Stubborn special rule.
Wargear:
• Cataphractii Terminator Armour
• Combi-plasma gun
• Two Power weapons
• Auspex
• Nuncio Vox
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)
• Hydra's Resilience</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="XX — ALPHARIUS, THE HYDRA" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="490" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra-cat" name="Lords of War" hidden="false" targetId="cat-low" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-xx" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra-unique" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Alpharius" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">7</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">6</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">1+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xx-10-xx-alpharius-the-hydra-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Primarch of the Alpha Legion, the Last Primarch, Lord of the XX Legion
Of all the Emperor’s sons, none was surrounded by as much uncertainty as Alpharius. Even within the Alpha Legion, identity was a weapon to be concealed, exchanged and discarded as readily as any blade. Warriors adopted their Primarch’s name and appearance, false commanders led genuine assaults, and seemingly insignificant operations concealed objectives whose importance became apparent only after victory had already been achieved.
Upon the battlefield Alpharius rarely presented the enemy with a single obvious centre of command. His plans were layered with feints, infiltrators and hidden contingencies, allowing the Primarch himself to remain unseen until the precise instant his presence would prove decisive. By the time the enemy understood which warrior truly bore the Pale Spear, the Hydra’s coils had usually closed around them.
Alpharius | 7 | 7 | 6 | 6 | 5 | 6 | 5 | 10 | 1+
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Alpharius
Unit Type:
• Infantry (Character)
Wargear:
• Pythian Scales
• Pale Spear
• Hydra’s Spite
• Frag Grenades
Special Rules:
• Primarch
• Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion)
• Master of Lies
• The Hydra
• Sire of the Alpha Legion
• I Am Alpharius
PYTHIAN SCALES The armour of Alpharius incorporated technologies whose origins and capabilities were known only to the inner circles of the XX Legion, its shifting surface and serpentine ornamentation concealing a defence worthy of a Primarch. The Pythian Scales count as Primarch Armour. PALE SPEAR The true origins of the Pale Spear were unknown, though the weapon was believed to be of Xenos manufacture and possessed destructive properties unlike those of the conventional weapons of the Imperium. The Pale Spear is a Two-Handed Power Weapon. Attacks made with the Pale Spear are resolved at Alpharius’ normal Strength and have the Armourbane special rule. Any unsaved Wound inflicted by the Pale Spear against a model without the Primarch special rule becomes a Massive Wound and inflicts D3 Wounds instead of one Wound. HYDRA’S SPITE Hydra’s Spite was an ancient plasma weapon of exceptional manufacture, its compact form concealing firepower sufficient to destroy even heavily armoured warriors. Weapon Range S AP Type Hydra’s Spite 18" 7 2 Assault 2, Gets Hot MASTER OF LIES Few commanders could distinguish the true deployment of the XX Legion from the feints and false dispositions which surrounded it. After both armies have deployed but before the first turn begins, nominate one friendly Alpha Legion unit. That unit may be redeployed anywhere it could legally have been deployed at the beginning of the battle. It must obey all normal deployment restrictions and may not be placed into Reserve unless it was already eligible to begin the battle in Reserve. THE HYDRA Every operation of the Alpha Legion concealed objectives within objectives, the destruction of a seemingly insignificant target often revealing itself as the purpose around which the entire battle had been constructed. Before either army deploys, secretly record one enemy unit as the Alpha Legion’s Priority Target. The identity of the Priority Target need not be revealed until the first time a friendly Alpha Legion unit makes an attack against it. Once revealed, friendly units with the Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) special rule may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1 when attacking the Priority Target. This applies to both shooting and close combat attacks. SIRE OF THE ALPHA LEGION The warriors of the XX Legion operated according to plans whose true scope was often known only to their Primarch, but the appearance of Alpharius upon the battlefield signalled that those plans had reached their decisive stage. Friendly units with the Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) special rule with at least one model within 12" of Alpharius may use his Leadership characteristic when taking Morale or Pinning tests. I AM ALPHARIUS The Alpha Legion cultivated deliberate uncertainty concerning the appearance and identity of its Primarch. Any warrior might be Alpharius, and an enemy could never be certain that the commander before them was truly the master of the XX Legion until it was already too late. Alpharius is not deployed normally and does not begin the battle in Reserve. At the beginning of any Alpha Legion turn, nominate one friendly Infantry model on the battlefield with the Legiones Astartes (Alpha Legion) special rule. Remove that model from play and replace it with Alpharius, placing Alpharius as close as possible to the model’s previous position. The replaced model counts as a casualty. Alpharius enters play with his full starting Wounds and all of his normal wargear and special rules. He does not retain any weapons, wargear, Wounds or other rules possessed by the model he replaced. If the replaced model was part of a unit, Alpharius immediately joins that unit. If the replaced model was engaged in close combat, Alpharius is considered engaged in the same close combat. Alpharius may Move, Shoot and declare charges normally during the turn in which he is revealed. No Reserve roll is required. If Alpharius has not been revealed when the battle ends, he counts as having been slain for the purposes of Victory Points, Slay the Warlord and Price of Failure. PRIMARCH RETINUE Alpharius may select any one of the following as his Primarch Retinue: • Legion Honour Guard Squad • Legion Terminator Command Squad • Lernaean Terminator Squad A retinue selected in this manner does not occupy an additional Force Organisation selection and otherwise follows the normal Primarch Retinue rules. Because Alpharius does not begin the battle on the battlefield, his Primarch Retinue deploys normally without him. Alpharius may use I Am Alpharius to replace a model in his Primarch Retinue. If he does so, he immediately joins that unit. A Lernaean Terminator Squad selected as Alpharius’ Primarch Retinue does not count against the normal 0–1 limitation on Lernaean Terminator Squads.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="KAKOPHONI SQUAD" hidden="true" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad"><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="150" /></ns0:costs><ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:categoryLink id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-cat" name="Troops" hidden="false" targetId="cat-troops" primary="true" /></ns0:categoryLinks><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="legion-iii" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="allegiance-traitor" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier><ns0:modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-hide"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" childId="r25-rite-iii-1-3rd-company-elite" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers><ns0:profiles><ns0:profile name="Kakophoni" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-profile-0"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile><ns0:profile name="Cacophonic Champion" typeId="prof-model" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-profile-1"><ns0:characteristics><ns0:characteristic name="WS" typeId="model-ws">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="BS" typeId="model-bs">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="S" typeId="model-s">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="T" typeId="model-t">4</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="W" typeId="model-w">1</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="I" typeId="model-i">5</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="A" typeId="model-a">2</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Ld" typeId="model-ld">10</ns0:characteristic><ns0:characteristic name="Sv" typeId="model-sv">3+</ns0:characteristic></ns0:characteristics></ns0:profile></ns0:profiles><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Source Entry" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-source" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Kakophoni | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 5 | 1 | 10 | 3+
Cacophonic Champion | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 5 | 2 | 10 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Heavy Support
CACOPHONY If an enemy unit suffers one or more casualties from shooting attacks made by a Kakophoni Squad, it must take a Pinning test after the squad has finished firing.
Unit Composition:
• 5 Kakophoni
• 1 Cacophonic Champion
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Cacophonic Champion is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Sonic Blaster
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Emperor's Children)
• Fearless
• Cacophony
Restriction:
• Traitor armies only
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to six additional Kakophoni
for +25 points per model.
• For every three models in the squad, one Kakophoni may replace his Sonic Blaster with:
• Blastmaster .................................. +15 points
• The Cacophonic Champion may replace his Sonic Blaster with:
• Doom Siren and bolt pistol .................. Free
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades .............................. +2 points per model
• The Cacophonic Champion may take:
• Power weapon ................................. +10 points
• Power fist ................................... +15 points
• Melta bombs .................................. +5 points
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
A squad of ten models or fewer may select a Rhino, Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-rite-note" name="Rite of War Interaction" hidden="false"><ns0:description>TRAITOR ONLY
As the III Legion descended into corruption, entire formations embraced the experimental sonic augmentations first developed amongst the Kakophoni. The most infamous of these formations was the 3rd Company, whose warriors willingly submitted themselves to increasingly extreme surgical and sonic modification.
EFFECTS
CHOSEN OF VAIROSEAN
Kakophoni Squads may be selected as Troops choices. Kakophoni Squads selected as Troops may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
All Kakophoni Squads in the Detachment gain the Relentless special rule.
SONIC ASSAULT
Any Emperor's Children Infantry unit composed entirely of models wearing Power Armour or Artificer Armour may purchase Sonic Shriekers for +2 points per model. Every eligible model in the unit must purchase the upgrade.
A unit equipped in this manner follows the normal Sonic Shrieker rules.
ARMOURY OF EXCESS
The normal restriction allowing only one Legion Heavy Support Squad to select Sonic Weaponry is removed.
Up to two Legion Heavy Support Squads may select Sonic Weaponry when using this Rite of War.
PERFECT CACOPHONY
A unit in which every surviving model is equipped with either a Sonic Weapon or Sonic Shrieker gains the Fear special rule.
LIMITATIONS
This Rite of War may only be selected by a Traitor Emperor's Children Detachment.
The army must include at least one Kakophoni Squad.
The army's Warlord must either:
• be equipped with a Sonic Shrieker; or
• be a named Character whose rules specifically associate him with the Kakophoni or 3rd Company.
The army may include no more than one Fortification.</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-clone-cleanup" name="Builder compatibility" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Removed 1 obsolete armoury link(s) inherited from the generic source entry while creating this Rite-specific battlefield-role copy.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="model" import="true" name="Additional model" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-additional"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-additional-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="6" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Additional model" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-additional-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>May include up to 6 additional models at +25 points each, as stated in the source entry.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntryGroups><ns0:selectionEntryGroup name="Options" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-options" collective="false" import="true"><ns0:selectionEntries><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="for" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-0-for"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-0-for-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="25" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-0-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The squad may include up to six additional Kakophoni</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Blastmaster" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-1-blastmaster"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-1-blastmaster-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="4" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="15" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-1-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• For every three models in the squad, one Kakophoni may replace his Sonic Blaster with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Doom Siren and bolt pistol" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-2-doom-siren-and-bolt-pistol"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-2-doom-siren-and-bolt-pistol-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="0" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-2-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The Cacophonic Champion may replace his Sonic Blaster with:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Krak grenades (base unit; +2 pts/model)" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-3-krak-grenades"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-3-krak-grenades-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="12" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-3-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The entire squad may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule name="Squad-wide cost note" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-3-squadwide" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The source prices this option at +2 points per model. The displayed selection charges the parsed base unit only; apply the same per-model surcharge for any additional models selected.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Power weapon" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-4-power-weapon"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-4-power-weapon-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="10" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-4-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The Cacophonic Champion may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Power fist" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-5-power-fist"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-5-power-fist-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="15" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-5-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The Cacophonic Champion may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Melta bombs" hidden="false" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-6-melta-bombs"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-6-melta-bombs-max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" type="max" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:costs><ns0:cost name="Points" typeId="pts" value="5" /></ns0:costs><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Option restriction" id="r42-role-iii-1-effects-chosen-of-vairosean-kakophoni-squads-r41-unit-iii-2-kakophoni-squad-opt-6-context" hidden="false"><ns0:description>• The Cacophonic Champion may take:</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries></ns0:selectionEntryGroup></ns0:selectionEntryGroups></ns0:selectionEntry><ns0:selectionEntry type="unit" name="0–1 Legion Artillery Tank Squadron" id="r42-role-iv-1-legion-artillery-tank-squadron-hs-artillery" hidden="true" import="true">
      <ns0:categoryLinks>
        <ns0:categoryLink id="r42-role-iv-1-legion-artillery-tank-squadron-hs-artillery-cat" name="Troops" hidden="false" targetId="cat-troops" primary="true" /></ns0:categoryLinks>
      <ns0:constraints>
        <ns0:constraint id="r42-role-iv-1-legion-artillery-tank-squadron-hs-artillery-roster-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" />
      </ns0:constraints>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule name="Squadron Composition" id="r42-role-iv-1-legion-artillery-tank-squadron-hs-artillery-comp" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>1–3 vehicles. Every vehicle in the squadron must be of the same type.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
        <ns0:rule name="New Recruit note" id="r42-role-iv-1-legion-artillery-tank-squadron-hs-art-note" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>For a two- or three-vehicle squadron, select the appropriate number of Additional vehicles. Vehicle upgrades and pintle weapons may be selected in matching quantities up to the number of vehicles in the squadron; do not assign more than one copy of a given upgrade to the same vehicle.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      <ns0:rule id="r42-role-iv-1-legion-artillery-tank-squadron-rite-note" name="Rite of War Interaction" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The Ironfire is a siege doctrine in which artillery fire is advanced across the battlefield immediately ahead of the Legion's assault formations.
Iron Warriors infantry advance through explosions, collapsing structures and clouds of debris, trusting their gunners to place each successive salvo only metres ahead of their position.
EFFECTS
ARTILLERY COLUMN
One Legion Artillery Tank Squadron may be selected as a non-compulsory Troops choice.
An Artillery Tank Squadron selected in this manner:
• does not occupy a Heavy Support choice;
• may not fulfil a compulsory Troops selection;
• does not count as a Scoring Unit unless it would normally do so for another reason.
The normal 0–1 restriction on Legion Artillery Tank Squadrons still applies.
ROLLING BOMBARDMENT
When an Iron Warriors Barrage weapon fires at a point within 12" of a friendly Iron Warriors unit, reduce its scatter distance.
If the attack would normally scatter 2D6", it scatters only D6" instead.
After resolving the Barrage attack, place an Ironfire Marker at the final centre point of the Blast marker.
WALKING THE FIRE
When another Iron Warriors Barrage weapon fires, it does not scatter if the initial target point is:
• within 18" of an Ironfire Marker; AND
• within 6" of a friendly Iron Warriors unit.
After resolving the attack, place a new Ironfire Marker at the centre of the Blast marker as normal.
If an Iron Warriors Shooting phase ends without a new Ironfire Marker being placed, remove all Ironfire Markers from the battlefield.
RIDE THE IRONFIRE
Iron Warriors Infantry units with at least one model within 6" of an Ironfire Marker gain the Fearless special rule.
This benefit lasts only while at least one model in the unit remains within 6" of an Ironfire Marker.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must possess the Master of the Legion special rule.
The army must contain at least one unit equipped with a Barrage weapon.
If the mission designates one player as the Attacker and the other as the Defender, the Iron Warriors must be the Attacker.
The army may not include a Fortification.</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule id="r42-role-iv-1-legion-artillery-tank-squadron-clone-cleanup" name="Builder compatibility" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Removed 1 obsolete armoury link(s) inherited from the generic source entry while creating this Rite-specific battlefield-role copy.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules>
