      <ns0:selectionEntry id="r42-role-v-0-effects-ride-like-the-wind-legion-sky-hunter-jetbike-squadrons-r37-rapid-fa-sky-hunter" name="Rapid Encirclement (Sky Hunter Phalanx)" type="upgrade" hidden="true" import="true"><ns0:constraints><ns0:constraint id="r42-role-v-0-effects-ride-like-the-wind-legion-sky-hunter-jetbike-squadrons-r37-rapid-fa-sky-hunter-max" type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" /></ns0:constraints><ns0:rules><ns0:rule name="Rapid Encirclement" id="r42-role-v-0-effects-ride-like-the-wind-legion-sky-hunter-jetbike-squadrons-r37-rapid-fa-sky-hunter-rule" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Once per battle, during its Movement phase, if every model in this unit can move completely off a table edge, remove the unit and place it into Ongoing Reserves. It returns during the controlling player’s following turn using the normal Outflank rules.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules><ns0:modifiers><ns0:modifier type="set" value="false" field="hidden"><ns0:conditions><ns0:condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="rite-skyhunter" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" /></ns0:conditions></ns0:modifier></ns0:modifiers></ns0:selectionEntry></ns0:selectionEntries>
      <ns0:rules>
        <ns0:rule name="Standard Wargear" id="r42-role-v-0-effects-ride-like-the-wind-legion-sky-hunter-jetbike-squadrons-fa-sky-std" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>Power Armour; Legion Scimitar Jetbike with Heavy Bolter; Bolt Pistol; Chainsword; Frag Grenades.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
        <ns0:rule name="Legiones Astartes &amp; Deep Strike" id="r42-role-v-0-effects-ride-like-the-wind-legion-sky-hunter-jetbike-squadrons-fa-sky-la" hidden="false">
          <ns0:description>Legiones Astartes and Deep Strike. The unit also has And They Shall Know No Fear as presented in ProHammer Classic and is not Fearless.</ns0:description>
        </ns0:rule>
      <ns0:rule id="r42-role-v-0-effects-ride-like-the-wind-legion-sky-hunter-jetbike-squadrons-rite-note" name="Rite of War Interaction" hidden="false"><ns0:description>The Chogorian Brotherhood is the archetypal war formation of the V Legion: a rapidly moving host of mounted warriors supported by mobile infantry and reconnaissance elements, striking from unexpected directions before disappearing beyond retaliation.
EFFECTS
RIDE LIKE THE WIND
Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons may be selected as Troops choices.
Legion Bike Squadrons and Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons may fulfil compulsory Troops selections.
LIGHTNING ENCIRCLEMENT
The following White Scars units gain the Outflank special rule:
• Legion Bike Squadrons
• Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons
• Legion Attack Bike Squadrons
• Legion Land Speeder Squadrons
• Javelin Attack Speeder Squadrons
In addition, White Scars Infantry units gain Outflank provided that the unit contains no model wearing Terminator Armour or carrying a Heavy weapon. A Dedicated Transport purchased for a unit deploying by Outflank may enter play with that unit.
MASTER OF THE HUNT
The White Scars player may re-roll Reserve rolls for units in this Detachment. The player may choose to re-roll either a successful or failed Reserve roll. The second result must be accepted.
STRIKE AND VANISH
A White Scars Bike or Jetbike unit which successfully uses Hit &amp; Run may roll one additional D6 for its Hit &amp; Run movement and discard the lowest result.
LIMITATIONS
The army's Warlord must be mounted on either:
• a Space Marine Bike; or
• a Jetbike.
The army's compulsory Troops choices must be Legion Bike Squadrons or Legion Sky Hunter Jetbike Squadrons.
The army may include no more than one Heavy Support choice. If every Bike and Jetbike unit in the Detachment has been completely destroyed by the end of the battle, the enemy receives an additional 150 Victory Points. This penalty only applies in missions using Victory Points.</ns0:description></ns0:rule><ns0:rule id="r42-role-v-0-effects-ride-like-the-wind-legion-sky-hunter-jetbike-squadrons-clone-cleanup" name="Builder compatibility" hidden="false"><ns0:description>Removed 2 obsolete armoury link(s) inherited from the generic source entry while creating this Rite-specific battlefield-role copy.</ns0:description></ns0:rule></ns0:rules>
